E["npc:jaina-proudmoore"] = {t="npc",n="Jaina Proudmoore",z="dustwallow",s="On Theramore Isle, Jaina Proudmoore works to preserve peace between the Alliance and the New Horde. Once a gifted student of Dalaran’s Kirin Tor, she led Lordaeron’s survivors across the Great Sea and now rules the island as its most powerful human sorceress.",h="On Theramore Isle, Jaina Proudmoore works to preserve peace between the Alliance and the New Horde.",sec={{t="Flight to Kalimdor",b="Jaina Proudmoore, daughter of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore of Kul Tiras, showed an early gift for magic. In Dalaran, she studied under Archmage Antonidas. During the Third War, she investigated the Plague of Undeath with Prince Arthas Menethil and witnessed Lordaeron’s fall.\n\nThen the Prophet Medivh warned her of the coming danger, and she gathered human survivors to sail west for Kalimdor. There, Jaina’s forces joined Thrall’s Horde and the night elves. Together they stood at Mount Hyjal, defeated Archimonde, and broke the Burning Legion’s invasion.",sp=0},{t="The Lady of Theramore",b="After the Legion’s defeat, Jaina founded Theramore, an island citadel off the coast of Dustwallow Marsh. It became the Alliance’s main stronghold in southern Kalimdor. Her commitment to peace faced its greatest test when her father came seeking vengeance against the orcs.\n\nJaina would not join his war. She stood aside as Thrall’s forces killed the Grand Admiral, preventing another devastating conflict in Kalimdor. Now Jaina rules Theramore and speaks for coexistence. She works closely with Warchief Thrall while holding the Alliance’s ground amid rising local tensions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lady Jaina Proudmoore?",a="Jaina rules Theramore Isle and is considered the most gifted living human mage. She is the daughter of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore of Kul Tiras and studied under Archmage Antonidas in Dalaran.",al={"who is jaina","jaina proudmoore lore","theramore leader"}},{q="Why is Jaina in Kalimdor instead of the Eastern Kingdoms?",a="Before Lordaeron fell in the Third War, the Prophet Medivh warned Jaina to lead as many people as she could across the sea to Kalimdor. Her expedition survived the voyage, fought at Mount Hyjal, and settled in Theramore, a port-fortress in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"why did jaina leave lordaeron","jaina kalimdor","why is theramore here"}},{q="What is Jaina's relationship with the Horde?",a="Jaina and Warchief Thrall share a cautious friendship. They fought together against the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal and have worked to keep peace between their peoples, despite fierce opposition from hardliners on both sides.",al={"is jaina friendly with thrall","jaina and horde","does jaina hate orcs"}},{q="What happened between Jaina and Prince Arthas Menethil?",a="Jaina and Arthas were close companions and shared a romance. They investigated the plague spreading across Lordaeron together, but Jaina was horrified as Arthas grew ruthless. At Stratholme, she refused to join him in slaughtering infected citizens.",al={"jaina and arthas","did jaina love arthas"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Jaina trained under Archmage Antonidas and is widely considered the most powerful living human sorceress. Her skill reflects the heights of Dalaran’s arcane mastery.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you have a vital foothold in southern Kalimdor through Jaina. She balances loyalty to Highlord Bolvar’s regency in Stormwind with her wish to avoid war with the neighboring Horde."},kw={"antonidas","arthas","dustwallow","jaina","kirin tor","proudmoore","theramore","thrall"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:dalaran","topic:new-horde","topic:burning-legion","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:medivh","topic:kul-tiras","topic:third-war"},src={"Jaina Proudmoore"}}
E["npc:nat-pagle"] = {t="npc",n="Nat Pagle",z="dustwallow",s="On a quiet inlet in Dustwallow Marsh, Nat Pagle fishes and teaches anglers who have proved their patience. He calls fishing an excuse to drink, yet anglers across Azeroth know his mastery.",h="On a quiet inlet in Dustwallow Marsh, Nat Pagle fishes and teaches anglers who have proved their patience.",sec={{t="The Master Angler",b="For decades, Nat Pagle has fished the waters of Azeroth. He speaks of the craft without much reverence, calling it a handy excuse to sit back and drink. Yet he knows aquatic life and angling better than anyone alive. He also licenses fishing gear sought by professionals.",sp=0},{t="A Marshland Hermit",b="Nat Pagle makes camp on a small spit along Dustwallow Marsh’s eastern coast, far from the taverns of the Eastern Kingdoms. He keeps clear of faction politics. Alliance travelers sent by trainers such as Grimnur Stonebrand come to him, and so do Horde anglers directed by Lumak in Orgrimmar. Anyone searching the world for rare specimens can earn a lesson from Nat.",sp=0},{t="Old Tales and Sea Monsters",b="Nat Pagle once ventured into the ruins of Zul'Gurub. Near waters prowled by the monstrous hydra Gahz'ranka, he misplaced his favorite measuring tape and tackle box.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nat Pagle?",a="Across Azeroth, anglers know Nat Pagle as the most famous fisherman. After decades on the water, he lives on the coast of Dustwallow Marsh and trains experienced anglers who have outgrown ordinary trainers.",al={"who is nat","nat pagle lore","who is the fishing guy"}},{q="Where can Nat Pagle be found?",a="Nat Pagle lives on a small spit of land on Dustwallow Marsh’s eastern coast in Kalimdor, southwest of Theramore Isle.",al={"where is nat pagle","nat pagle location","find nat pagle"}},{q="Why does Nat Pagle fish if he says he dislikes it?",a="Nat Pagle says fishing gives him a respectable, quiet excuse to sit by the water and drink for hours.",al={"does nat like fishing","why does nat fish","nat pagle drinking"}},{q="Will Nat Pagle train members of the Horde?",a="Yes. Nat Pagle takes no side in faction rivalries. His friend Lumak in Orgrimmar sends Horde anglers who have reached the limits of ordinary training to him.",al={"is nat alliance only","horde nat pagle","can horde talk to nat"}},{q="What connection does Nat Pagle have to Zul'Gurub?",a="Nat Pagle once fished in the ancient troll city of Zul'Gurub. He left his tackle box and favorite measuring tape near waters where the great hydra Gahz'ranka dwells.",al={"nat in zg","nat pagle tackle box","nat pagle zul gurub"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde angler, Lumak, the fishing trainer in Orgrimmar’s Valley of Honor, may send you south. He trusts Nat Pagle and sends promising fishermen to train with him.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance angler, a master such as Grimnur Stonebrand in Ironforge may send you to Dustwallow Marsh. Experienced fishermen go to Nat to learn the craft’s final secrets."},kw={"artisan fishing","dustwallow marsh","gahz'ranka","grimnur stonebrand","lumak","nat pagle","pagle","pagle's pointe"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","quest:6608","subzone:zul-gurub","zone:ironforge","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Nat Pagle"}}
E["npc:onyxia"] = {t="npc",n="Onyxia",z="dustwallow",s="In Dustwallow Marsh, Onyxia tends her brood and schemes to bring the mortal realms under black dragonflight rule. She is Deathwing’s daughter, while her brother Nefarian gathers armies in Blackrock Spire.",h="In Dustwallow Marsh, Onyxia tends her brood and schemes to bring the mortal realms under black dragonflight...",sec={{t="The Broodmother in the Court",b="Onyxia seeks power through guile while her brother Nefarian gathers armies in Blackrock Spire. Disguised as Lady Katrana Prestor, she has entered Stormwind’s highest noble circles. Trusted by the House of Nobles, she withholds soldiers and supplies from outposts in Westfall, Redridge, and the Burning Steppes. Her choices weaken the kingdom’s military and leave the mortal realms defenseless.",sp=1},{t="Architect of Ruin",b="Lady Katrana Prestor hides a predator’s cunning behind a painted smile. King Varian has gone missing on the way to a peace summit at Theramore. Prestor now holds deep influence over the young boy-king Anduin and has ensnared Highlord Bolvar Fordragon. The throne lies at the edge of her talons.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who is Lady Katrana Prestor?",a="Lady Katrana Prestor is a noblewoman of Stormwind and a trusted adviser at court. With King Varian missing, she stands beside the boy-king Anduin and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep. Her counsel carries great weight with the House of Nobles.",al={"prestor identity","who is prestor","katrana prestor real identity"},sp=2,it="identity"},{q="Why does Onyxia target Stormwind?",a="Onyxia seeks to bring Stormwind under the black dragonflight’s sway, weaken its military power, and aid her brother Nefarian’s dominion over the region.",al={"onyxia goal","why attack stormwind","prestor motive"},sp=2,it="why_here"},{q="Where does Onyxia live?",a="Onyxia lives in a subterranean lair in the swamps of Dustwallow Marsh, where she tends the clutches of her black dragonflight.",al={"where is onyxia","onyxia location","onyxia lair location"},sp=2,it="place"},{q="What is her connection to Nefarian and Deathwing?",a="Onyxia is Deathwing’s daughter and Nefarian’s younger sister. She works closely with him to restore the black dragonflight’s supremacy across Azeroth.",al={"onyxia brother","onyxia father","onyxia family"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Onyxia on?",a="Onyxia belongs solely to the black dragonflight and serves the dark designs of her family. Allied closely with her brother Nefarian, she works to rebuild their corrupted flight and subjugate the mortal races. She owes no allegiance to the Alliance or Horde; mortal kingdoms exist only to be manipulated, weakened, and broken to ensure black dragon supremacy.",al={"onyxia side","who does onyxia serve","onyxia faction","onyxia alliance or horde"},it="side",add="fd0ec0c3"},{q="What does Onyxia want?",a="Onyxia seeks to bring the Kingdom of Stormwind under the black dragonflight's sway. She works to weaken its armies and leave the realm defenseless, so that her brood and her brother Nefarian's forces can rise unchallenged.",al={"what does onyxia want","onyxia goal","onyxia motive","what is onyxias plan"},it="wants",add="d77da3f3"},{q="Why is Onyxia so feared?",a="As the daughter of Deathwing and broodmother of the black dragonflight, Onyxia is as deadly in physical might as she is in cunning. Though comparatively small for a mature dragon, her strikes are lightning-quick, and her fiery breath can melt iron within moments. Combined with her insidious talent for weaving deception among mortals, she poses an existential threat to Azeroth.",al={"why is onyxia feared","is onyxia powerful","onyxia reputation"},it="fame",add="ba62a202"}},kw={"anduin wrynn","black dragonflight","bolvar fordragon","deathwing","nefarian","onyxia","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:onyxia-s-lair","topic:black-dragonflight","zone:stormwind","npc:deathwing","topic:house-of-nobles","topic:varian-wrynn","topic:defias-brotherhood"},src={"Onyxia"}}
E["npc:overlord-mok-morokk"] = {t="npc",n="Overlord Mok'Morokk",z="dustwallow",s="Brackenwall Village is where Overlord Mok'Morokk rules the Stonemaul ogres of Dustwallow Marsh. Rexxar chose him for his strength, but now he is a tyrant who will not defend his clan from the black dragonflight.",h="Brackenwall Village is where Overlord Mok'Morokk rules the Stonemaul ogres of Dustwallow Marsh.",sec={{t="A Tyrant in the Marsh",b="Rexxar defeated Kor'gall, the former chieftain, and led the Stonemaul clan in defense of Durotar. When he left, he put Mok'Morokk in command, trusting his strength in battle. He was wrong to trust him. Mok'Morokk chose intimidation and comfort over care for his kin. From Brackenwall Village, he demands tribute he has not earned and bullies anyone who questions his rule.",sp=0},{t="The Coward of Brackenwall",b="The black dragonflight descended on ancestral Stonemaul Village. Many ogres died, and the survivors were driven into Brackenwall's muck. Mok'Morokk forbade his clan to act. Fear of the dragons kept him from rallying a counterattack or avenging the dead. His advisers have grown discontent. Draz'Zilb, an ogre mage, and others quietly seek champions from beyond the clan to challenge Mok'Morokk's rule.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Overlord Mok'Morokk?",a="Mok'Morokk rules the Stonemaul ogres from Brackenwall Village in Dustwallow Marsh. Rexxar named him leader, but he soon grew selfish and demanding.",al={"who is mok'morokk","brackenwall leader","stonemaul ogre boss"}},{q="How did Mok'Morokk become leader of the Stonemaul clan?",a="Rexxar defeated the Stonemaul clan's former leader and took command during the founding of Durotar. When Rexxar left to wander the wilderness, he appointed Mok'Morokk overlord for his raw physical strength.",al={"how did mok'morokk get in charge","rexxar chose mok'morokk","why is he chieftain"}},{q="Why are the Stonemaul ogres in Brackenwall Village?",a="The Stonemaul ogres lived in Stonemaul Village until black dragons attacked and razed it. The survivors fled north into the swamps and made Brackenwall Village their refuge.",al={"why did ogres move to brackenwall","what happened to stonemaul village","black dragon attack ogres"}},{q="Why won't Mok'Morokk fight the black dragonflight?",a="Mok'Morokk is terrified of the dragons despite his size and fierce reputation. He refuses to lead a counterattack for his clan's ancestral territory. Instead, he sits idle in Brackenwall, hoards tribute, and ignores his people's cries.",al={"why doesn't mok'morokk fight dragons","is mok'morokk a coward","retake stonemaul"}},{q="Do the other Stonemaul ogres respect Mok'Morokk?",a="The Stonemaul clan grows resentful of Mok'Morokk's laziness, cowardice, and bullying. His advisers worry about the clan's future under his rule.",al={"do ogres like mok'morokk","draz'zilb mok'morokk","stonemaul rebellion"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Rexxar's campaign brought the Stonemaul ogres into alliance with the Horde. Under Mok'Morokk's weak and cowardly rule, Brackenwall Village is vulnerable.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, Mok'Morokk shows how strength without honor or courage can turn to cowardice and tyranny."},kw={"brackenwall","draz'zilb","dustwallow","mok'morokk","ogre","overlord","rexxar","stonemaul"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","topic:black-dragonflight","topic:horde","zone:durotar","npc:onyxia"},src={"Overlord Mok'Morokk"}}
E["npc:tabetha"] = {t="npc",n="Tabetha",z="dustwallow",s="At her farmstead deep in the Quagmire, Tabetha teaches aspiring spellcasters and aids those seeking mastery of arcane and occult relics.",h="At her farmstead deep in the Quagmire, Tabetha teaches aspiring spellcasters and aids those seeking mastery...",sec={{t="Hermit of the Quagmire",b="North of the Stonemaul Ruins, Tabetha lives in a secluded shack with her apprentices. She chose solitude over the academic hierarchies of the Eastern Kingdoms. Spellcasters cross Kalimdor's beasts and mire to seek her guidance, drawn by her mastery of the arcane.",sp=0},{t="A Neutral Mentor",b="Tabetha welcomes Alliance and Horde initiates who are willing to learn. Though human, she teaches mages and helps warlocks with dangerous bindings such as the Orb of Orahil. Her history with Menara Voidrender reaches into esoteric magic beyond faction allegiance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Tabetha?",a="Tabetha lives at Tabetha's Farm, in a secluded shack deep in the Quagmire of western Dustwallow Marsh, just north of the Stonemaul Ruins.",al={"tabetha location","where is tabetha","tabetha farm map"}},{q="Is Tabetha hostile to Horde players?",a="No. Though human, Tabetha is neutral. She teaches apprentices and aids spellcasters from both the Horde and the Alliance.",al={"is tabetha alliance only","can horde talk to tabetha","tabetha faction"}},{q="Why do mages and warlocks seek her out?",a="Mages and warlocks seek Tabetha for her knowledge of arcane rituals, magical foci, and binding rites. Mages ask her about craft mastery and power trials, while warlocks seek help to cleanse or bind potent artifacts such as the Orb of Orahil.",al={"why visit tabetha","tabetha class quest","orb of orahil tabetha"}},{q="What is her connection to Menara Voidrender?",a="Tabetha shares a history with Menara Voidrender. Though their paths have diverged, their knowledge of powerful relics and binding magic connects them across their separate hermitages.",al={"tabetha and menara","menara voidrender history"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can turn to Tabetha for guidance as you test your grasp of arcane rituals and refine your craft in dangerous lands like Uldaman.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can turn to Tabetha for help with dangerous magical relics such as the Infernal Orb and the Orb of Orahil."},kw={"dustwallow marsh","mage quest","menara voidrender","orb of orahil","quagmire","tabetha","tabetha's farm"},rel={"subzone:tabetha-s-farm","zone:dustwallow","subzone:quagmire","npc:menara-voidrender","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","subzone:uldaman"},src={"Tabetha"}}
E["quest:1132"] = {t="quest",n="Fiora Longears",z="dustwallow",s="From Menethil Harbor, you sail west across the Great Sea to meet Fiora Longears in Theramore. Red Jack Flint sends you to his high elf contact at the town inn.",h="From Menethil Harbor, you sail west across the Great Sea to meet Fiora Longears in Theramore.",sec={{t="A Call to the West",b="Many humans, dwarves, and gnomes look upon the Eastern Kingdoms and see old conflicts and damaged earth. At Menethil Harbor, sailor Red Jack Flint urges travelers to board a ship across the Great Sea. He speaks of Kalimdor as an uncharted land of fortune and opportunity. Then he sends you to Theramore to meet his associate, the elf Fiora Longears.",sp=0},{t="Arrival in Theramore",b="Your voyage ends at Theramore, an Alliance port on the coast of Dustwallow Marsh. Fiora Longears waits at the town inn for travelers sent by Flint. She trusts his judgment of character and welcomes the Alliance heroes who have just arrived. From there, she prepares to guide you inland toward Ashenvale's ancient forests.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fiora Longears?",a="Fiora Longears is a high elf waiting in the inn at Theramore, in Dustwallow Marsh. Red Jack Flint's contact, she greets Alliance travelers arriving from the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"fiora longears","who is fiora"},it="identity"},{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Red Jack Flint, an energetic human sailor, offers the journey west from Menethil Harbor on the coast of the Wetlands.",al={"quest giver","where to get fiora longears quest","who gives quest"},gp=true},{q="How do I reach Fiora Longears from Menethil Harbor?",a="Board the passenger ship at Menethil Harbor and sail west across the Great Sea to Theramore in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"how to get to theramore","ship to theramore","boat from menethil"},gp=true},{q="What happens after meeting Fiora Longears?",a="Fiora welcomes you in Theramore and praises Flint's recommendation. She sends you inland to Astranaar in Ashenvale for the next part of your journey.",al={"what comes next","follow up quest","journey to astranaar quest"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the relationship between Red Jack Flint and Fiora Longears?",a="Flint calls Fiora his partner across the sea. He scouts eager adventurers in the Eastern Kingdoms, while Fiora receives them in Kalimdor and helps with Alliance operations and inland travel.",al={"are flint and fiora partners","red jack flint fiora connection"},it="ties"},{q="Why is the Alliance recruiting travelers to Kalimdor?",a="Kalimdor offers the Alliance vast new territory and resources. Night elven allies there need help defending their ancestral lands from threats such as the Horde and demonic remnants.",al={"why go to kalimdor","why theramore"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Red Jack Flint want to send you to Kalimdor?",a="Red Jack Flint sees himself as an agent of opportunity, tasked with inspiring promising adventurers in Menethil Harbor to cross the Great Sea. Bound to the docks himself and longing for ocean voyages, his role is to spot hardy souls and direct them to his high elf partner, Fiora Longears, who helps newcomers find their footing and take up the Alliance's burgeoning efforts across Kalimdor.",al={"red jack flint motive","why send me to fiora","why does jack flint want this done"},it="motive",add="869cd7aa"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, this journey links the Eastern Kingdoms with Kalimdor's night elven territories, joining the eastern and western frontiers.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you find Fiora Longears welcoming eastern allies in Theramore and preparing them for the ancient wilds of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"theramore","boat","dustwallow marsh","fiora longears","kalimdor","menethil harbor","red jack flint","wetlands"},rel={"npc:red-jack-flint","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:dustwallow","quest:1133","subzone:astranaar"},m={start="Red Jack Flint",["end"]="Fiora Longears",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1132},src={"Fiora Longears (quest)"}}
E["quest:1135"] = {t="quest",n="Highperch Venom",z="dustwallow",s="From Theramore, Fiora Longears sends hunters west for wyvern venom. At Highperch in Thousand Needles, the wyverns carry venom sacs buyers value across Kalimdor.",h="From Theramore, Fiora Longears sends hunters west for wyvern venom.",sec={{t="A Lucrative Expedition",b="In Theramore, Fiora Longears seeks hunters willing to travel far for a trade beyond the Horde’s use of wyverns as flying mounts. Buyers across Kalimdor value the creatures’ lethal venom, often more than the beasts themselves. The journey means dangerous heights and a hunt for fresh venom sacs.",sp=0},{t="The Crags of Highperch",b="Highperch lies west of Dustwallow Marsh, among the sandstone mesas of Thousand Needles. Its wyverns carry unusually concentrated toxin, but reaching their nests means crossing Horde territory and climbing treacherous ground. You must slay the wyverns and take their venom sacs intact, then carry them back to Theramore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find the wyverns for this quest?",a="The wyverns roost at Highperch, a tall mesa in western Thousand Needles, west of Theramore.",al={"highperch location","where is highperch","wyvern location"},gp=true},{q="Who is Fiora Longears?",a="Fiora Longears is an Alliance contact in Theramore, off the coast of Dustwallow Marsh. She recruits adventurers to gather rare and valuable natural reagents from across Kalimdor.",al={"fiora longears","who gives highperch venom"},it="identity"},{q="Why is wyvern venom so valuable?",a="Wyvern venom is potent and valued by select underground circles, apothecaries, and traders. The Horde prizes wyverns as flying mounts, while alchemists and poison-makers pay well for their venom glands.",al={"why wyvern venom","wyvern poison use"},it="power"},{q="Why is a Theramore quest sending me so far west?",a="Fiora seeks exotic specimens not found in the marshes around Theramore. Highperch in Thousand Needles is home to a distinct wyvern breed with concentrated venom.",al={"why thousand needles","why send to thousand needles"},it="place"},{q="What happens when you return the venom sacs?",a="Fiora inspects the sacs and says they are full of venom. She remarks that such quality usually comes from young wyverns or fertile females, then congratulates you on the hunt.",al={"fiora reaction","quest completion highperch venom"},it="next_step"},{q="Is Highperch safe for Alliance travelers?",a="No. Horde forces are numerous in Thousand Needles, with nearby settlements such as Freewind Post. Wild predators and hostile Horde scouts both threaten you at Highperch.",al={"is highperch dangerous","alliance in thousand needles"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Fiora Longears want this done?",a="Fiora has an eye for lucrative commerce and rare reagents. While most know wyverns only as beasts of burden tamed by the Horde, she knows that certain circles pay dearly for potent venom. Harvesting the sacs from Highperch allows her to turn a handsome profit in those specialized markets.",al={"why does fiora want venom","fiora longears motive","why harvest wyvern venom"},it="motive",add="9e43b6cb"},{q="What is the Highperch Venom Sac for?",a="The venom sacs contain the deadly, potent toxin of the wild wyverns that nest upon the heights of Thousand Needles. Highly prized by select alchemists, poisoners, and exotic traders, these bursting sacs fetch an enormous price in markets dealing in rare and dangerous beasts.",al={"what are highperch venom sacs for","venom sac use","why collect venom sacs"},it="item",add="ef763353"},{q="What are the creatures nesting at Highperch?",a="Highperch is a towering mesa in Thousand Needles that serves as a wild roost for native wyverns. Untamed and fiercely territorial, these winged predators glide the desert canyons, using their venomous stingers to fell prey before dragging meals up to their rocky aeries.",al={"what are highperch wyverns","who are you hunting at highperch","what live at highperch"},it="target",add="f9186ab4"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you understand the allure of exotic toxins. Handling pure wyvern venom gives you a close look at Kalimdor’s deadliest natural poisons.",["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you see how trade and curiosity about rare reagents reach beyond Ashenvale and Darkshore, deep into Thousand Needles’ arid barrens.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you venture deep into Horde territory in Thousand Needles, beneath the watch of tauren and orc patrols."},kw={"dustwallow marsh","fiora","highperch","longears","theramore","thousand needles","venom","wyvern"},rel={"quest:1132","subzone:highperch","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Fiora Longears",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1135,ri={"Highperch Venom Sac"}},src={"Highperch Venom"}}
E["quest:1166"] = {t="quest",n="Overlord Mok'Morokk's Concern",z="dustwallow",s="Overlord Mok'Morokk sends you south from Brackenwall Village to recover what he left at the Stonemaul clan's old home. He wants his grog, snuff and strongbox back.",h="Overlord Mok'Morokk sends you south from Brackenwall Village to recover what he left at the Stonemaul clan's...",sec={{t="The Overlord's Story",b="Mok'Morokk says Rexxar made him the mighty leader of the Stonemaul clan. He says he keeps his people safe. When big dragons came to the clan's old home and brought fire, he found them a new home here in Dustwallow.",sp=0},{t="Things Left Behind",b="Mok'Morokk left the old home in such a hurry that he forgot his grog, snuff and strongbox. He points you south to the Den of Flame and the Stonemaul Ruins, certain his things are there. He says he is too busy leading the ogres to go himself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Overlord Mok'Morokk?",a="Overlord Mok'Morokk leads the Stonemaul clan from Brackenwall Village. He says Rexxar made him its mighty leader.",al={"mok'morokk","ogre leader","who is the overlord"}},{q="What happened to the Stonemaul clan's old home?",a="Mok'Morokk says big dragons came to the Stonemaul clan's old home and brought fire. So he found the clan a new home in Brackenwall Village.",al={"why did ogres leave","stonemaul destroyed","dragons attack ogres"}},{q="What does Mok'Morokk want back?",a="Mok'Morokk wants his grog, snuff and strongbox back. He forgot them when he left the old home in a hurry.",al={"mok'morokk items","what things does he want","grog snuff strongbox"}},{q="Where are Mok'Morokk's belongings?",a="Mok'Morokk sends you south, certain his belongings are in the Den of Flame and the Stonemaul Ruins.",al={"where are the items","item locations","find grog and snuff"}},{q="Why doesn't Mok'Morokk fetch his things himself?",a="Mok'Morokk says he is too busy leading the ogres to fetch his things himself.",al={"why doesn't mok'morokk go","why send me"}}},kw={"brackenwall","den of flame","dustwallow","grog","mok'morokk","rexxar","snuff","stonemaul","strongbox"},rel={"npc:overlord-mok-morokk","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","subzone:den-of-flame","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Overlord Mok'Morokk",["end"]="Overlord Mok'Morokk",level="43",id=1166},src={"Overlord Mok'Morokk's Concern","Classic quest text: Overlord Mok'Morokk's Concern"}}
E["quest:1168"] = {t="quest",n="Army of the Black Dragon",z="dustwallow",s="In Brackenwall Village, the Army of the Black Dragon has left Tharg grieving and thirsting for vengeance. He blames Overlord Mok'Morokk for ordering the ogres to flee.",h="In Brackenwall Village, the Army of the Black Dragon has left Tharg grieving and thirsting for vengeance.",sec={{t="A Grievance of Blood",b="Black dragons killed Tharg's wife along with many ogres. After Rexxar made Mok'Morokk Overlord, the new leader ordered the survivors to run until they reached Brackenwall Village. Tharg says ogres are poor at running and should fight instead. He believes Mok'Morokk thinks only of himself, though Mok'Morokk now tells all ogres to stay put and keep Brackenwall Village safe.",sp=0},{t="Home in the South",b="Tharg calls the Stonemaul Ruins his home and likes the south. Brackenwall Village is no home to him. He wants revenge on the black dragon army and a return to the ruins, so he asks you to cut down Firemane Scouts and Firemane Ash Tails among its ranks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tharg?",a="Tharg is an ogre living in Brackenwall Village. Black dragons killed his wife, and he seeks revenge and a return to the Stonemaul Ruins.",al={"tharg lore","who is tharg","tharg dustwallow"}},{q="Why does Tharg dislike Overlord Mok'Morokk?",a="Rexxar made Mok'Morokk Overlord, but Tharg believes he cares more for himself than for the ogres. When black dragons killed many ogres, Mok'Morokk ordered the survivors to run. Tharg believes ogres should fight.",al={"why tharg hate mok morokk","mok'morokk coward","tharg and mok morokk"}},{q="What happened to Tharg's wife?",a="Black dragons killed Tharg's wife along with many other ogres. Her death fuels his wish for revenge.",al={"thargs wife","what happened to thargs wife","tharg wife dead"}},{q="Where is the ogres' old home?",a="Tharg calls the Stonemaul Ruins his home and likes the south. Brackenwall Village is not home to him, and he wants to return to the ruins.",al={"stonemaul ogre home","where did ogres come from","stonemaul ruins history"}},{q="Which enemies make up the army of the black dragon?",a="Tharg points you toward the Firemane, including Firemane Scouts and Firemane Ash Tails.",al={"firemane dragonkin","who to kill army of black dragon","firemane enemies"}}},kw={"brackenwall","dustwallow","firemane","mok'morokk","rexxar","stonemaul","tharg"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Tharg",["end"]="Tharg",level="43",faction="Horde",id=1168},src={"Army of the Black Dragon"}}
E["quest:1169"] = {t="quest",n="Identifying the Brood",z="dustwallow",s="In Brackenwall Village, Draz'Zilb seeks the beast that attacked the clan's old home. Draz'Zilb says Mok'Morokk clings to power while Tharg struggles with sorrow and vengeance, and asks you for fifteen searing tongues and fifteen searing hearts.",h="In Brackenwall Village, Draz'Zilb seeks the beast that attacked the clan's old home.",sec={{t="A Voice of Reason",b="Draz'Zilb says Mok'Morokk is consumed by power while Tharg wrestles with sorrow and a thirst for vengeance. In Draz'Zilb's view, no one else is trying to learn who attacked the clan's old home. The ogre speaks with care, though you might have expected a brute's words.",sp=0},{t="Hearts and Tongues",b="Draz'Zilb asks you to take fifteen tongues and fifteen hearts from the whelps and hatchlings. The burned young belong to the black dragon army, and Draz'Zilb hopes their remains will reveal which beast sent her young into the ogres' home.\n\nIf the ogres learn what kind of beast they face, they may destroy their enemy for good and reclaim Stonemaul Village from ruin. Draz'Zilb says getting Mok'Morokk to leave the swamp will be a great labor of its own.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Draz'Zilb?",a="Draz'Zilb is an ogre in Brackenwall Village who speaks formally rather than like a brute. Draz'Zilb wants to learn who attacked the clan's old home.",al={"drazzilb","ogre mage brackenwall","smart ogre"}},{q="What does Draz'Zilb want from the whelps and hatchlings?",a="Draz'Zilb asks for fifteen searing tongues and fifteen searing hearts from the whelps and hatchlings. Their remains may reveal which beast sent her young into the old home.",al={"searing hearts use","why tongues and hearts","identifying the brood purpose"}},{q="What does Draz'Zilb think of the clan's leaders?",a="Draz'Zilb has little respect for Mok'Morokk, whom the ogre calls a craven fool consumed by power. Draz'Zilb sees Tharg as caught in sorrow and a thirst for revenge.",al={"mokmorokk problem","tharg and mokmorokk","stonemaul leaders"}}},kw={"black dragon","brackenwall village","draz'zilb","dustwallow marsh","mok'morokk","searing hearts","searing tongues","stonemaul","tharg"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Draz'Zilb",["end"]="Draz'Zilb",level="43",id=1169},src={"Classic quest text: Identifying the Brood"}}
E["quest:1170"] = {t="quest",n="The Brood of Onyxia",z="dustwallow",s="Draz'Zilb fears Onyxia's brood has come for more than a siege against a few ogres.",h="Draz'Zilb fears Onyxia's brood has come for more than a siege against a few ogres.",sec={{t="A Troubling Presence",b="Draz'Zilb reports that Onyxia's brood has invaded Stonemaul Village. Onyxia is Deathwing's daughter, and her arrival troubles him. He is certain the brood seeks more than a siege against a few ogres. So you carry word to Overlord Mok'Morokk in Brackenwall Village, where he can take action.",sp=0},{t="Word at Brackenwall",b="Overlord Mok'Morokk does not welcome news of the brood at Stonemaul Village. He dislikes dragons, so he prefers Brackenwall Village and insists there are no dragons here.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Overlord Mok'Morokk?",a="Draz'Zilb sends you to Overlord Mok'Morokk after Onyxia's brood invades Stonemaul Village.",al={"who starts the brood of onyxia","brood of onyxia quest giver"}},{q="Where can Overlord Mok'Morokk be found?",a="Overlord Mok'Morokk can be found in Brackenwall Village.",al={"mok'morokk location","where is mok'morokk","overlord mok'morokk dustwallow"}},{q="Why is Draz'Zilb concerned about Onyxia's brood?",a="Draz'Zilb wonders why Deathwing's daughter came to these lands. He is certain she came for more than a siege against a small band of ogres.",al={"why does draz'zilb care about dragons","draz'zilb onyxia concern"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","deathwing","draz'zilb","dustwallow marsh","mok'morokk","onyxia","stonemaul"},rel={"npc:overlord-mok-morokk","subzone:brackenwall-village","npc:onyxia","npc:deathwing","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Draz'Zilb",["end"]="Overlord Mok'Morokk",level="43",faction="Horde",id=1170},src={"The Brood of Onyxia"}}
E["quest:1171"] = {t="quest",n="The Brood of Onyxia",z="dustwallow",s="At Brackenwall Village, The Brood of Onyxia meets Overlord Mok'Morokk's denial. He says no black dragons are here and sends you back to Draz'Zilb with word that the ogres will stay.",h="At Brackenwall Village, The Brood of Onyxia meets Overlord Mok'Morokk's denial.",sec={{t="Leave Me Alone",b="Overlord Mok'Morokk wants to be left alone after Draz'Zilb reports the brood of Onyxia. He says the ogres will stay where they are and denies that any black dragon is here. Carry his answer to Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village.",sp=0},{t="What Draz'Zilb Says",b="Draz'Zilb calls Overlord Mok'Morokk a lazy coward and says something must be done. Mok'Morokk showed strength while Rexxar led the ogres. After Rexxar departed, power tempted him. Now Mok'Morokk demands service from the ogres instead of leading them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Overlord Mok'Morokk refuse to act?",a="Overlord Mok'Morokk refuses to act because he says there are no black dragons here and wants to be left alone. He sends you to tell Draz'Zilb that the ogres will stay.",al={"why mok'morokk not help","mok'morokk reaction","why no black dragons"}},{q="What comes before this in the storyline?",a="This follows the earlier account of The Brood of Onyxia, when Draz'Zilb sent you to bring word of the brood to Mok'Morokk.",al={"what comes before this quest","quest chain order"}},{q="Where does this take place?",a="Overlord Mok'Morokk and Draz'Zilb are both in Brackenwall Village.",al={"where is this quest","location"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","brood of onyxia","draz'zilb","dustwallow marsh","mok'morokk","rexxar"},rel={"npc:overlord-mok-morokk","quest:1170","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow","npc:onyxia"},m={start="Overlord Mok'Morokk",["end"]="Draz'Zilb",level="43",faction="Horde",id=1171},src={"The Brood of Onyxia (2)"}}
E["quest:1172"] = {t="quest",n="The Brood of Onyxia",z="dustwallow",s="In the marsh's south, Draz'Zilb sends you against Onyxia's eggs. No more of her whelps should hatch.",h="In the marsh's south, Draz'Zilb sends you against Onyxia's eggs.",sec={{t="The Eggs in the Wyrmbog",b="Onyxia's brood lies scattered through the Dragonmurk. Draz'Zilb urges you south to the Wyrmbog, where the ogre is sure Onyxia made her lair and scattered her eggs. Dragons nest in the land around Stonemaul Village, keeping the ogres from taking it back. So you are sent to find and destroy the eggs.",sp=0},{t="One Last Service",b="When the eggs are destroyed, Draz'Zilb says Onyxia will need some time before she can lay more. The ogre thanks you on behalf of the Stonemaul Clan. Then Draz'Zilb asks one last service. Mok'Morokk is unfit to lead, but Tharg, who would make an excellent leader, is held back by injuries and age. Drive Mok'Morokk out by force, and a new leader can bring the clan back to its proper home in the south.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village sends you to destroy Onyxia's eggs.",al={"who gives the brood of onyxia","quest giver brood of onyxia","drazzilb quest"}},{q="Why must the dragon eggs be destroyed?",a="Draz'Zilb wants no more of Onyxia's whelps to hatch. While dragons nest in the land around Stonemaul Village, the ogres cannot take it back.",al={"why destroy onyxia eggs","why smash eggs","stonemaul village dragon eggs"}},{q="Where are the eggs located?",a="The eggs are around the Wyrmbog in the marsh's south. Draz'Zilb is sure Onyxia made her lair there.",al={"where are onyxia eggs","egg of onyxia location","where is wyrmbog"}},{q="Where does this step fit in the broader chain?",a="This follows Mok'Morokk's refusal to act on news of the brood. You carried his answer back to Draz'Zilb.",al={"brood of onyxia chain","previous quest brood of onyxia","what comes before brood of onyxia 3"}}},kw={"brackenwall","brood of onyxia","dragonmurk","draz'zilb","mok'morokk","onyxia","stonemaul","wyrmbog"},rel={"quest:1170","quest:1171","npc:onyxia","subzone:wyrmbog","subzone:dragonmurk","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Draz'Zilb",["end"]="Draz'Zilb",level="45",faction="Horde",id=1172},src={"The Brood of Onyxia (3)"}}
E["quest:1173"] = {t="quest",n="Challenge Overlord Mok'Morokk",z="dustwallow",s="In Brackenwall Village, Overlord Mok'Morokk laughs at your challenge and vows to crush you. Draz'Zilb expected you to drive him from the village.",h="In Brackenwall Village, Overlord Mok'Morokk laughs at your challenge and vows to crush you.",sec={{t="A Challenge to the Overlord",b="After The Brood of Onyxia, you face Overlord Mok'Morokk. He laughs at your nerve and promises to crush you. Then he tells you to speak when you are ready for a beating. Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village expected you to chase Mok'Morokk from the village. Why have you returned only to talk?",sp=0},{t="Word for Draz'Zilb",b="Draz'Zilb says Mok'Morokk fled like a coward after you won the fight. He thanks you for a great service. With Mok'Morokk gone, the ogres can choose a new leader to help them take back their old home for good.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who do you challenge?",a="You challenge Overlord Mok'Morokk in Brackenwall Village. He laughs and boasts that he will crush you.",al={"who do i fight","challenge target","who is mok'morokk"}},{q="What comes before this challenge?",a="The Brood of Onyxia comes before your challenge.",al={"what quest comes before this","prerequisite quest","previous quest"}},{q="Who do you report to after the fight?",a="After the fight, you report to Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village.",al={"who do i turn this in to","turn in npc","where to go after beating mok'morokk"}},{q="What does Draz'Zilb expect of you?",a="Draz'Zilb expects you to chase Mok'Morokk from the village. He wonders why you returned only to talk.",al={"why fight mok'morokk","why challenge the overlord","reason for the fight"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","challenge overlord mok'morokk","draz'zilb","dustwallow marsh","mok'morokk","stonemaul"},rel={"npc:overlord-mok-morokk","quest:1172","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Overlord Mok'Morokk",["end"]="Draz'Zilb",level="45",id=1173},src={"Classic quest text: Challenge Overlord Mok'Morokk"}}
E["quest:1177"] = {t="quest",n="Hungry!",z="dustwallow",s="Mudcrush Durtfeet is hungry in northern Dustwallow Marsh and wants food from you. Bash the fishy Mirefin and bring back their heads, or Mud will eat you.",h="Mudcrush Durtfeet is hungry in northern Dustwallow Marsh and wants food from you.",sec={{t="A Hungry Ogre",b="Mudcrush Durtfeet, an ogre called Mud, makes a plain bargain. Bash the fishy Mirefin and bring him their heads for food. Feed Mud, or he will eat you.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mudcrush Durtfeet?",a="Mudcrush Durtfeet is a big ogre in northern Dustwallow Marsh, and he goes by Mud. He is hungry and wants food.",al={"mudcrush durtfeet","who is mudcrush","ogre in dustwallow"}},{q="What does Mudcrush Durtfeet want to eat?",a="Mud wants heads from the fishy Mirefin you are told to bash.",al={"mudcrush food","what does the ogre want","hungry quest food"}},{q="What happens if you refuse to feed him?",a="Mud makes the choice plain: feed him, or he will eat you.",al={"mudcrush threat","will mudcrush eat me"}}},kw={"dustwallow marsh","fishy","hungry!","mirefin heads","mudcrush durtfeet","ogre"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Mudcrush Durtfeet",["end"]="Mudcrush Durtfeet",level="36",id=1177},src={"Hungry!"}}
E["quest:1201"] = {t="quest",n="Theramore Spies",z="dustwallow",s="In Dustwallow, Horde and Alliance keep an uneasy truce, though skirmishes and covert deeds continue. Nazeer Bloodpike wants Alliance infiltrators east of Brackenwall Village hunted down and slain.",h="In Dustwallow, Horde and Alliance keep an uneasy truce, though skirmishes and covert deeds continue.",sec={{t="Spies East of the Village",b="Alliance spies watch Brackenwall Village from the islands to its east. They send word of Horde movements back to Theramore.\n\nNazeer Bloodpike, the village spymaster, sends you to find and kill them. Their superiors must know such spies are unwelcome.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders the death of the Theramore infiltrators?",a="Nazeer Bloodpike, the spymaster in Brackenwall Village, orders the infiltrators killed.",al={"who gives quest theramore spies","nazeer bloodpike spy quest","who starts theramore spies"}},{q="Where are the infiltrators hiding?",a="The infiltrators hide on the islands east of Brackenwall Village.",al={"theramore infiltrators location","where to find theramore spies","infiltrator locations dustwallow"}},{q="Why are the spies watching Brackenwall Village?",a="The spies watch Brackenwall Village and send word of Horde movements back to Theramore.",al={"why are humans spying on brackenwall","brackenwall village spies motive"}},{q="What comes after dealing with the spies?",a="The next step is The Theramore Docks.",al={"theramore spies follow up","what quest comes after theramore spies"}}},kw={"brackenwall","dustwallow","infiltrators","nazeer bloodpike","spies","theramore"},rel={"quest:1202","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={start="Nazeer Bloodpike",["end"]="Nazeer Bloodpike",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1201},src={"Theramore Spies"}}
E["quest:1202"] = {t="quest",n="The Theramore Docks",z="dustwallow",s="At Theramore Docks, papers taken from a ship lie beneath the water. Nazeer Bloodpike sends you to recover them after two spies were discovered and cast them into the sea.",h="At Theramore Docks, papers taken from a ship lie beneath the water.",sec={{t="Papers in the Water",b="After dealing with the Theramore spies, you hear from Nazeer Bloodpike again. Two spies went to a ship by the Theramore docks and took its papers. They were discovered and threw the papers into the sea. One spy escaped and reported the failure, unable to retrieve what they had cast away.",sp=0},{t="Beneath the Docks",b="The Captain's Documents lie in a footlocker beneath the water by the Theramore docks. You are sent to recover them and bring them to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village. He says the papers matter greatly to the Alliance's stability. That makes them important to the Horde's security, too.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Theramore Isle?",a="Nazeer Bloodpike sends you from Brackenwall Village.",al={"who gives the quest","where does this quest start","quest giver"}},{q="What are you looking for beneath the docks?",a="You are looking for a footlocker beneath the Theramore docks. It holds the Captain's Documents.",al={"what do i need to find","what item is in the water","docks objective"}},{q="Why were the documents thrown into the water?",a="The two spies took papers from a ship at the docks, but were discovered and forced to throw them into the sea. One escaped without them.",al={"why are the papers in the ocean","how did the footlocker get there","why did the spies drop it"}},{q="Why does the Horde want these documents?",a="Nazeer Bloodpike says the documents matter greatly to the Alliance's stability, and therefore to the Horde's security.",al={"why are the papers important","what is in the documents","why does bloodpike want them"}},{q="What comes before this in the storyline?",a="It follows Theramore Spies, where you hunted the infiltrators east of Brackenwall Village.",al={"prerequisite quest","previous quest","what leads to this"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","captain's documents","docks","dustwallow marsh","footlocker","nazeer bloodpike","spies","theramore"},rel={"quest:1201","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={start="Nazeer Bloodpike",["end"]="Nazeer Bloodpike",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1202},src={"The Theramore Docks"}}
E["quest:1203"] = {t="quest",n="Jarl Needs a Blade",z="dustwallow",s="In Dustwallow Marsh, Jarl needs a blade for urgent cutting. “Swamp Eye” Jarl wants a moonsteel broadsword and warns you not to dawdle.",h="In Dustwallow Marsh, Jarl needs a blade for urgent cutting.",sec={{t="A Certain Blade",b="“Swamp Eye” Jarl has cutting to do, but keeps its purpose to himself. He asks for a particular blade, called a moonsteel broadsword by some and a swing blade by Jarl. You might find one in town, or ask a blacksmith to make one special. Jarl warns you not to sleep on it; whatever needs cutting will not keep forever.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the blade?",a="“Swamp Eye” Jarl is asking for the blade in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"who gives jarl needs a blade","who is jarl","swamp eye jarl"}},{q="What weapon does Jarl require?",a="Jarl requires a moonsteel broadsword, which Jarl calls a swing blade.",al={"what sword does jarl want","jarl weapon","which blade does jarl need"}},{q="Why does Jarl need a blade so urgently?",a="Jarl has cutting to do but will not say what needs cutting. Jarl warns that it will not keep forever.",al={"why does jarl need a blade","what is jarl cutting","jarl purpose"}},{q="Where does Jarl suggest finding the sword?",a="Jarl says you might find one in town or ask a blacksmith to make one special.",al={"how to get moonsteel broadsword for jarl","where to find blade for jarl"}}},kw={"dustwallow marsh","jarl","moonsteel broadsword","swamp eye jarl","swing blade"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},m={start="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl",["end"]="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl",level="35",id=1203},src={"Jarl Needs a Blade (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1204"] = {t="quest",n="Mudrock Soup and Bugs",z="dustwallow",s="In Theramore, Morgan Stern hopes to win Stormwind City over with a new dish. The trek through Dustwallow Marsh is too much for Morgan Stern, so you gather Mudrock tongues for Mudrock Soup and Bugs.",h="In Theramore, Morgan Stern hopes to win Stormwind City over with a new dish.",sec={{t="A Dish in the Making",b="Morgan Stern is gathering ingredients for a new dish in Theramore. A long trek through Dustwallow Marsh is more than Morgan Stern expects to survive, so you hunt Mudrock turtles. Their tongues are needed first.",sp=0},{t="Forked Tongues",b="Mudrock turtles roam the coast of Dustwallow Marsh, mostly around the bay. Morgan Stern wants forked tongues in particular, having heard they bring a distinct flavor to the dish.",sp=0},{t="Toward the Table",b="Morgan Stern will try different ways of cooking the tongues to find what best brings out their taste. Morgan Stern hopes to make a dish fit for the Blue Recluse in Stormwind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the turtle tongues?",a="Morgan Stern, in Theramore, is making a dish called Mudrock Soup and Bugs.",al={"who starts mudrock soup and bugs","morgan stern theramore"}},{q="Where can the Mudrock turtles be found?",a="Mudrock turtles roam along the coast of Dustwallow Marsh, mostly around the bay.",al={"mudrock turtle location","where are mudrocks"}},{q="Why does Morgan Stern want forked tongues specifically?",a="Morgan Stern has heard forked tongues carry a distinct flavor wanted in the dish.",al={"why forked tongues","forked mudrock tongues reason"}},{q="Why won't Morgan Stern gather the ingredients in person?",a="Morgan Stern doubts they would survive a long trek through Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"why doesnt morgan stern hunt","morgan stern marsh"}},{q="What comes after this quest?",a="The next step is called ... and Bugs.",al={"next quest after mudrock soup","mudrock soup follow up"}}},kw={"blue recluse","bugs","dustwallow marsh","forked tongues","morgan stern","mudrock","soup","theramore"},rel={"quest:1258","zone:dustwallow","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Morgan Stern",["end"]="Morgan Stern",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=1204},src={"Mudrock Soup and Bugs"}}
E["quest:1206"] = {t="quest",n="Jarl Needs Eyes",z="dustwallow",s="At Swamplight Manor, Jarl seeks forty unpopped Darkmist eyes for their smooth, salty juice. The spiders live in Darkmist Cavern, west of the manor.",h="At Swamplight Manor, Jarl seeks forty unpopped Darkmist eyes for their smooth, salty juice.",sec={{t="A Taste for Spider Eyes",b="After Soothing Spices, Jarl turns to eye juice, a drink they enjoy. Most creatures have only two eyes, but spiders have many. Jarl likes the taste of Darkmist eye juice. The Darkmist spiders live in Darkmist Cavern, west of the manor. Jarl wonders whether the cave took its name from the spiders, or the spiders from the cave.",sp=0},{t="A Feast for Jarl",b="Jarl welcomes the eyes and calls them tasty. They say to save for last any eyes that stare back when stared at, since they can keep a person company in the swamp. Then Jarl greets the little eyes, tastes them, and says they are like gooey, salty chicken.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks for the spider eyes?",a="“Swamp Eye” Jarl asks for the eyes at Swamplight Manor in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"who gives this quest","jarl quest giver","swamp eye jarl"}},{q="Why does Jarl want spider eyes?",a="Jarl enjoys drinking eye juice and likes Darkmist eye juice for its smooth, salty taste. Most creatures have only two eyes, while spiders have many.",al={"why spider eyes","what does jarl do with eyes","eye juice"}},{q="Where are the Darkmist spiders?",a="The Darkmist spiders live in Darkmist Cavern, west of Swamplight Manor.",al={"darkmist cavern location","where are darkmist spiders","where to find eyes"}},{q="How many eyes does Jarl want?",a="Jarl wants forty unpopped Darkmist eyes.",al={"how many eyes","eye count"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="Soothing Spices came first.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite","what leads to this"}}},kw={"darkmist","darkmist cavern","dustwallow marsh","jarl","spider eyes","swamp eye jarl","swamplight manor"},rel={"subzone:swamplight-manor","subzone:darkmist-cavern","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl",["end"]="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl",level="35",id=1206},src={"Classic quest text: Jarl Needs Eyes"}}
E["quest:1218"] = {t="quest",n="Soothing Spices",z="dustwallow",s="In Dustwallow Marsh, \"Swamp Eye\" Jarl needs three Soothing Spices for a stew.",h="In Dustwallow Marsh, \"Swamp Eye\" Jarl needs three Soothing Spices for a stew.",sec={{t="Spice for the Pot",b="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl loves swamp cooking, including fried green frog legs. Now Jarl plans a stew and needs soothing spice for the pot. Bring three Soothing Spices, and Jarl will share the stew with you. Does stew suit your taste?",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants the soothing spices?",a="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl wants the soothing spices. Jarl is found in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"who gives soothing spices","quest giver soothing spices","swamp eye jarl spices"}},{q="What does Swamp Eye Jarl intend to cook with the spices?",a="Jarl plans to cook a stew with the spices and share it with you. Jarl enjoys swamp cooking, including fried green frog legs.",al={"what does jarl make","what stew does jarl make","jarl food"}},{q="How many spices does Jarl need?",a="Jarl needs three Soothing Spices.",al={"how many soothing spices","soothing spices count","soothing spices requirement"}}},kw={"dustwallow marsh","frog legs","soothing spices","stew","swamp eye jarl"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},m={start="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl",["end"]="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl",level="35",id=1218},src={"Soothing Spices (quest)"}}
E["quest:1219"] = {t="quest",n="The Orc Report",z="dustwallow",s="In Dustwallow Marsh, you find a severed orc hand gripping a bone tube. Inside lies a dirt-stained parchment in Orcish, meant for a Theramore Lieutenant.",h="In Dustwallow Marsh, you find a severed orc hand gripping a bone tube.",sec={{t="A Hand in the Dirt",b="In the loose dirt, you find a severed orc hand gripping a tube carved from bone. Inside is a dirt-stained parchment written in Orcish. It seems significant, and a Theramore Lieutenant is the one to show it to.",sp=0},{t="The Lieutenant's Verdict",b="The Theramore Lieutenant admits to reading Orcish poorly. Still, the lieutenant takes the parchment for an orc spy's report.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is hidden in the loose dirt?",a="In the loose dirt, you find a severed orc hand clutching a tube carved from bone. Inside is a dirt-stained parchment.",al={"what do you find in loose dirt","loose dirt item","orc hand in dustwallow"}},{q="Who should get the parchment?",a="A Theramore Lieutenant should receive the parchment.",al={"where do I take the report","who gets the spy report","theramore lieutenant location"}},{q="What language is the parchment written in?",a="The parchment is written in Orcish, and its writing seems significant.",al={"parchment language","can I read the parchment"}}},kw={"bone tube","dustwallow marsh","loose dirt","orc report","theramore lieutenant"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Loose Dirt",["end"]="Theramore Lieutenant",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=1219},src={"Classic quest text: The Orc Report"}}
E["quest:1220"] = {t="quest",n="Captain Vimes",z="dustwallow",s="Near Theramore, Lieutenant Aden sends you to Captain Garran Vimes with an orc report and word of Horde spies.",h="Near Theramore, Lieutenant Aden sends you to Captain Garran Vimes with an orc report and word of Horde spies.",sec={{t="A Report for the Captain",b="Lieutenant Aden sends you to Captain Garran Vimes with the orc report you found. Vimes reads orcish better than most, so Aden wants him to know that Horde spies are close to Theramore. You’ll find Vimes at the barracks on the northeastern side of Theramore Isle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Captain Vimes?",a="Lieutenant Aden sends you, hoping Captain Vimes will read the orc report you found.",al={"who starts captain vimes","where do i get captain vimes"}},{q="Where is Captain Garran Vimes located?",a="Captain Garran Vimes is at the barracks on Theramore Isle’s northeastern side.",al={"where is captain vimes","captain vimes location","vimes barracks"}},{q="Why does Captain Vimes need to see the report?",a="Aden says Vimes reads orcish better than most. He wants Vimes to hear that Horde spies are close to Theramore.",al={"why captain vimes","why does vimes need the report"}}},kw={"captain vimes","dustwallow marsh","garran vimes","lieutenant aden","orc report","spy's report","theramore","theramore isle"},rel={"subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","topic:horde"},m={start="Lieutenant Aden",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=1220},src={"Captain Vimes"}}
E["quest:1222"] = {t="quest",n="Stinky's Escape",z="dustwallow",s="In the swamp, \"Stinky\" Ignatz is searching for bogbean leaves for a cook in Theramore. Critters have surrounded him, and he asks you to guard him while he looks for a plant. When he is done, Morgan Stern is waiting in Theramore.",h="In the swamp, \"Stinky\" Ignatz is searching for bogbean leaves for a cook in Theramore.",sec={{t="Surrounded",b="\"Stinky\" Ignatz is glad to find someone who does not see him as a meal. Morgan Stern, a cook in Theramore, sent him to gather bogbean leaves for a new recipe. Ignatz guesses Stern finds them tasty. Now critters have surrounded him, and he asks you to guard his back while he searches for a bogbean plant.",sp=0},{t="A Cook Waiting",b="Morgan Stern, a cook in Theramore, is anxious. Ignatz went into the swamp a while ago and has not returned.",sp=0},{t="Thanks from the Cook",b="Morgan Stern says Ignatz brought the bogbean leaves and told him how you helped through trouble. To thank you, Stern will ask an uncle to give you a feast the next time you visit the Blue Recluse in Stormwind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is \"Stinky\" Ignatz?",a="Morgan Stern, a cook, sent \"Stinky\" Ignatz into the swamp to gather bogbean leaves.",al={"stinky ignatz","who is stinky","ignatz dustwallow"}},{q="Why is Ignatz in trouble?",a="Critters surrounded Ignatz while he searched for a bogbean plant.",al={"why is stinky trapped","ignatz stranded","why is stinky in dustwallow"}},{q="What are bogbean leaves for?",a="Morgan Stern is working on a new recipe and sent Ignatz to gather bogbean leaves. Ignatz guesses Stern finds them tasty.",al={"bogbean leaves","what are bogbeans","bogbean plant"}},{q="Who is Morgan Stern?",a="Morgan Stern is a cook in Theramore, and he is working on a new recipe.",al={"morgan stern theramore","who is morgan stern","cook morgan stern"}}},kw={"blue recluse","bogbean","dustwallow marsh","morgan stern","stinky ignatz","theramore"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","quest:1271"},m={start="\"Stinky\" Ignatz",["end"]="Morgan Stern",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=1222},src={"Classic quest text: Stinky's Escape"}}
E["quest:1238"] = {t="quest",n="The Lost Report",z="dustwallow",s="In Dustwallow Marsh, you uncover a spy's report bound for Brackenwall Village. An orc's severed hand grips a bone tube holding a dirt-stained account of weeks spent watching Theramore.",h="In Dustwallow Marsh, you uncover a spy's report bound for Brackenwall Village.",sec={{t="A Hand in the Dirt",b="You find an orc's severed hand in loose dirt, its fingers closed around a tube carved from bone. Inside lies a dirt-stained parchment. It reports on Theramore after weeks of spying and is meant for Nazeer Bloodpike, the orcs' spymaster at Brackenwall Village.",sp=0},{t="Word from the Spymaster",b="Nazeer Bloodpike names Marg Nighteye as the report's author. Marg was an agent stationed outside Theramore to watch the city. This is Marg's latest report, and perhaps the last. From what you tell him, Bloodpike fears Marg met an end in the swamp.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the report found?",a="You find the report in loose dirt in Dustwallow Marsh, clutched by a severed orc hand.",al={"where is the report","lost report location","how to start the lost report"}},{q="What is the report about?",a="An orc wrote the report after spying on Theramore for weeks.",al={"what is in the report","what does the spy report say","parchment contents"}},{q="Who gets the report?",a="The report goes to Nazeer Bloodpike, the orcs' spymaster at Brackenwall Village.",al={"who do i turn the report in to","lost report turn in","where to bring spy report"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","dustwallow marsh","loose dirt","nazeer bloodpike","spy report","the lost report","theramore"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Loose Dirt",["end"]="Nazeer Bloodpike",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1238},src={"Classic quest text: The Lost Report"}}
E["quest:1239"] = {t="quest",n="The Severed Head",z="dustwallow",s="In Dustwallow Marsh, you uncover a male orc's severed head. Bring it to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.",h="In Dustwallow Marsh, you uncover a male orc's severed head.",sec={{t="A Grim Find",b="Your digging turns up a male orc's head, ragged where it was cut from the neck. Its lips curl in a snarl, and dark eyes glare defiantly. Bring the head to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.",sp=0},{t="Nazeer Looks Closer",b="Nazeer Bloodpike recognizes Marg Nighteye's head at once, though he had feared Marg was dead. The ragged wound leaves him wondering whether a weapon made the cut or a beast killed the agent. Nazeer wants to solve the mystery and learn whether the Alliance was behind Marg's death.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do you bring the severed head?",a="Bring the severed head to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.",al={"where to turn in severed head","severed head turn in","who takes the head"}},{q="What does the head look like?",a="It is a male orc's head, ragged where it was cut from the neck, with lips drawn in a snarl and dark eyes glaring defiantly.",al={"what is in the loose dirt","defiant orc head","severed head description"}},{q="What comes after the severed head?",a="The next step is The Troll Witchdoctor.",al={"next quest after severed head","severed head followup"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","defiant orc head","dustwallow marsh","loose dirt","marg nighteye","nazeer bloodpike","severed head"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow","quest:1240","topic:alliance"},m={start="Loose Dirt",["end"]="Nazeer Bloodpike",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1239},src={"The Severed Head"}}
E["quest:1240"] = {t="quest",n="The Troll Witchdoctor",z="dustwallow",s="Nazeer Bloodpike seeks the truth about Marg Nighteye's death through troll witch-magic. You carry Marg's head to Kin'weelay at Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",h="Nazeer Bloodpike seeks the truth about Marg Nighteye's death through troll witch-magic.",sec={{t="Witch-Magic of the Trolls",b="Nazeer Bloodpike insists the truth about Marg's death must come to light. He says only troll witch-magic can reveal what happened. So you carry Marg's head to Kin'weelay at Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale. No Darkspear witchdoctor is mightier than Kin'weelay, and Nazeer believes Kin'weelay can reach Marg's spirit.",sp=0},{t="Words at Grom'gol",b="At Grom'gol, Kin'weelay senses an angry spirit. The witchdoctor studies the head and sees that the orc's spirit remains bound to this world. It rages over a duty left undone. Kin'weelay proposes to speak with it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why must Marg Nighteye's head be taken to Stranglethorn Vale?",a="Nazeer Bloodpike says only troll witch-magic can reveal what happened around Marg Nighteye's death. Kin'weelay is at Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"why go to stranglethorn","why grom'gol","why kin'weelay"}},{q="Who is Kin'weelay?",a="Kin'weelay is the mightiest witchdoctor among the Darkspear trolls. Kin'weelay can be found at Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"who is the witchdoctor","witchdoctor kin'weelay"}},{q="What comes after this step?",a="Marg Speaks comes next.",al={"what quest is next","after the troll witchdoctor"}}},kw={"darkspear witchdoctor","defiant orc head","grom'gol base camp","kin'weelay","marg nighteye","nazeer bloodpike","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"npc:kin-weelay","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","zone:stranglethorn","quest:1239","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Nazeer Bloodpike",["end"]="Kin'weelay",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1240},src={"The Troll Witchdoctor"}}
E["quest:1251"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="At the burned Shady Rest Inn, a black shield clings to the crumbling chimney. Krog at Brackenwall Village waits to see it.",h="At the burned Shady Rest Inn, a black shield clings to the crumbling chimney.",sec={{t="A Shield on the Chimney",b="Fire swept through the Shady Rest Inn and left little behind. An iron shield, charred black, is fixed to the crumbling chimney. You can work it free of the brick and bring it to Krog at Brackenwall Village. He will ask whether it counts as evidence from the inn’s remains.",sp=0},{t="What Krog Makes of It",b="Krog grants that humans have odd tastes in decoration. Yet he doubts anyone would hang a plain iron shield over a fireplace. He suspects whoever set the inn ablaze left it there as a warning or a threat.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the black shield found?",a="The black shield is fixed to the chimney of the burned Shady Rest Inn, one of the few remnants of the building.",al={"black shield location","where is shield","shady rest inn shield"}},{q="Who gets the shield?",a="Bring the shield to Krog at Brackenwall Village.",al={"who wants the black shield","where to turn in shield","krog location"}},{q="Can the shield be taken from the chimney?",a="Yes. You can work the shield loose from the chimney’s brick.",al={"can i remove the shield","take shield off chimney"}}},kw={"black shield","blackened iron shield","brackenwall village","dustwallow marsh","krog","shady rest inn"},rel={"quest:1321","subzone:shady-rest-inn","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Black Shield",["end"]="Krog",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1251},src={"Classic quest text: The Black Shield"}}
E["quest:1252"] = {t="quest",n="Lieutenant Paval Reethe",z="dustwallow",s="At the Shady Rest Inn, Lieutenant Paval Reethe's badge lies beneath the rubble, marked with Theramore's sign. Bring it to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.",h="At the Shady Rest Inn, Lieutenant Paval Reethe's badge lies beneath the rubble, marked with Theramore's sign.",sec={{t="A Glint in the Rubble",b="Ash and debris bury a badge in the Shady Rest Inn ruins. Beneath it, Lieutenant Paval Reethe's name lies below Theramore's sign. Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore asks what you found, and the badge belongs in his hands.",sp=0},{t="The Captain's Reply",b="Captain Garran Vimes says a guard's badge brings grim news. Some guards fall in battle, and he must carry word to their grieving families. Others vanish, leaving their fate unknown. At times, the truth is worse still.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the badge found?",a="The badge lies beneath rubble, ash, and debris in the Shady Rest Inn ruins. Captain Garran Vimes asks what you found there.",al={"badge location","where to find reethe badge","shady rest inn badge"}},{q="Whose name is on the badge?",a="Lieutenant Paval Reethe's name is embossed beneath the anchor.",al={"who is paval reethe","name on badge","who lost the badge"}},{q="Who gets the badge?",a="Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore should see the badge.",al={"who do i give the badge to","where to turn in badge","captain garran vimes location"}},{q="What does the badge look like?",a="The badge bears a gold anchor over white enamel, Theramore's sign.",al={"theramore symbol","guard badge appearance","what does the badge look like"}}},kw={"dustwallow marsh","garran vimes","paval reethe","shady rest inn","theramore guard badge"},rel={"quest:1259","subzone:shady-rest-inn","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Theramore Guard Badge",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=1252},src={"Classic quest text: Lieutenant Paval Reethe"}}
E["quest:1253"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="At the burned Shady Rest Inn, a fire-blackened shield hangs from the crumbling chimney. Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore awaits evidence from the ruins.",h="At the burned Shady Rest Inn, a fire-blackened shield hangs from the crumbling chimney.",sec={{t="A Shield on the Chimney",b="Few parts of the burned Shady Rest Inn remain beyond a crumbling chimney. A fire-blackened iron shield is still fixed to its brick, and can be removed. Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore awaits evidence from the inn site.",sp=0},{t="The Captain's Verdict",b="Captain Garran Vimes knows how arms and armor are used, though he does not claim to know how they are made. The shield looks ordinary to him, save for the damage left by the fire.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the black shield located?",a="The black shield is fixed to the brick of the crumbling chimney, one of the few parts of the burned Shady Rest Inn still standing.",al={"where is the shield","black shield location","find black shield"}},{q="Who wants evidence from the Shady Rest Inn?",a="Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore wants evidence from the Shady Rest Inn ruins.",al={"who wants the shield","shady rest investigator","who is garran vimes"}}},kw={"black shield","chimney","dustwallow marsh","garran vimes","iron shield","shady rest inn","theramore"},rel={"subzone:shady-rest-inn","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Black Shield",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=1253},src={"The Black Shield (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:1258"] = {t="quest",n="... and Bugs",z="dustwallow",s="Morgan Stern in Theramore is shaping a recipe that may become Stormwind's next food craze. He has the Mudrock tongues, but still needs pristine, unscarred legs from a giant crab.",h="Morgan Stern in Theramore is shaping a recipe that may become Stormwind's next food craze.",sec={{t="Legs Without a Scratch",b="Morgan Stern needs each crab leg's shell to shape his dish's appearance. Every leg must be pristine and unscarred, yet an adult crab may have only one or two legs fit for his research. He needs many, and the Muckshells of Dustwallow Marsh will not do. Only crabs from the faraway Swamp of Sorrows suit the recipe, so you face a long journey.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Morgan Stern?",a="Morgan Stern is in Theramore, shaping a recipe that may become Stormwind's next food craze.",al={"who is morgan stern","morgan stern theramore","who gives and bugs"}},{q="Where do the crab legs come from?",a="The legs must come from crabs in the faraway Swamp of Sorrows. The Muckshells of Dustwallow Marsh will not do for Morgan Stern's dish.",al={"where to find crawler legs","where are spiny rock crawlers","crawler legs location"}},{q="Why do the crab legs need to be pristine?",a="The crab leg shells shape the dish's appearance, so Morgan Stern needs legs without scars.",al={"why pristine crawler legs","why unscarred legs","crawler leg presentation"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="It follows Mudrock Soup and Bugs, the first part of your work for Morgan Stern's new recipe.",al={"previous quest and bugs","mudrock soup and bugs prerequisite"}}},kw={"crawler legs","dustwallow marsh","morgan stern","mudrock soup and bugs","pristine crawler leg","stormwind","theramore","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"quest:1204","subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Morgan Stern",["end"]="Morgan Stern",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=1258},src={"... and Bugs"}}
E["quest:1259"] = {t="quest",n="Lieutenant Paval Reethe",z="dustwallow",s="In Theramore, Captain Garran Vimes asks you to learn who Lieutenant Paval Reethe is.",h="In Theramore, Captain Garran Vimes asks you to learn who Lieutenant Paval Reethe is.",sec={{t="Who Is Reethe?",b="Captain Garran Vimes does not recognize Lieutenant Paval Reethe's name. So he sends you to Adjutant Tesoran in Theramore, who keeps the guard's records of its people and equipment. Vimes expects those records to reveal who Reethe is.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to find out about Reethe?",a="Captain Garran Vimes sends you to learn who Lieutenant Paval Reethe is. He does not recognize the name.",al={"who starts lieutenant paval reethe","reethe quest giver","who gives reethe quest"}},{q="Who keeps the Theramore guard's records?",a="Adjutant Tesoran in Theramore keeps records of the Theramore guard's people and equipment.",al={"where is adjutant tesoran","theramore records keeper","who has the guard books"}},{q="What can Adjutant Tesoran tell you?",a="Vimes expects Tesoran's records to reveal who Lieutenant Paval Reethe is.",al={"what does tesoran know","tesoran books"}}},kw={"adjutant tesoran","captain garran vimes","dustwallow marsh","paval reethe","theramore"},rel={"quest:1252","quest:1285","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Captain Garran Vimes",["end"]="Adjutant Tesoran",level="40",id=1259},src={"Classic quest text: Lieutenant Paval Reethe"}}
E["quest:1260"] = {t="quest",n="Morgan Stern",z="dustwallow",s="In Theramore, Angus Stern waits for word from Morgan Stern, who is gathering recipes for a new menu.",h="In Theramore, Angus Stern waits for word from Morgan Stern, who is gathering recipes for a new menu.",sec={{t="A Bayou Menu",b="Angus Stern wants customers at the Blue Recluse to taste rural dishes in the bayou style. He sent his nephew Morgan to Theramore, the city beside Dustwallow Marsh, to gather recipes from the locals. The journey is too long for Angus, so he asks you, a young traveler, to speak with Morgan.",sp=0},{t="What Morgan Has to Say",b="In Theramore, Morgan Stern says his search for recipes has brought him a few leads. He needs help following them, and the work calls for someone willing to get their feet wet.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Morgan Stern?",a="Morgan Stern is Angus Stern's nephew. Angus sent him to Theramore to gather recipes from the locals.",al={"who is morgan stern","morgan stern lore","angus stern nephew"}},{q="Why does Angus Stern want to reach Morgan?",a="Angus is developing a new menu of rural dishes with a bayou theme for the Blue Recluse. He wants to hear what Morgan has found so far.",al={"why send to theramore","blue recluse menu","angus stern quest"}},{q="Where can Morgan Stern be found?",a="Morgan is in Theramore, the city beside Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"where is morgan stern","morgan stern location","theramore chef location"}}},kw={"angus stern","bayou","blue recluse","dustwallow marsh","morgan stern","stormwind","theramore"},rel={"quest:1204","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Angus Stern",["end"]="Morgan Stern",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=1260},src={"Morgan Stern (quest)"}}
E["quest:1261"] = {t="quest",n="Marg Speaks",z="dustwallow",s="Near Theramore, Marg's stolen pendant and unfinished duty still weigh on them. Marg asks you to find the muckshell that killed them, recover the jeweled pendant taken from Alliance soldiers, and carry it to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.",h="Near Theramore, Marg's stolen pendant and unfinished duty still weigh on them.",sec={{t="What Marg Saw Near Theramore",b="Alliance soldiers had made camp on the beach near Theramore. One wore a pendant set with more gems than a soldier could pay for. Marg slipped into the camp that night and stole it. On the way back to base, a muckshell crab-man killed Marg. Now Marg asks you to find the muckshell, recover the pendant, and bring it to Nazeer in Brackenwall Village.",sp=0},{t="What Nazeer Makes of It",b="Nazeer is startled that a Stormwind soldier wore the pendant. You have learned how Marg died, yet the pendant raises a new question. Nazeer warns that it may bring dire effects to both the Alliance and the Horde.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Marg and how did Marg die?",a="Marg stole a jeweled pendant from Alliance soldiers camped near Theramore. A muckshell crab-man killed Marg on the way back to base.",al={"how did marg die","who is marg","marg story"}},{q="Where did the jeweled pendant come from?",a="An Alliance soldier wore the pendant at a beach camp near Theramore. It held more gems than a soldier could pay for, and Marg stole it that night.",al={"where did the pendant come from","who had the pendant","marg pendant origin"}},{q="Who receives the recovered pendant?",a="Nazeer Bloodpike receives the recovered pendant in Brackenwall Village.",al={"who gets the pendant","where do i take the pendant","nazeer bloodpike pendant"}},{q="What comes directly before this quest?",a="It follows The Troll Witchdoctor.",al={"previous quest","what quest comes before marg speaks"}}},kw={"bloodpike","brackenwall","marg","muckshell","nazeer","pendant","stormwind","theramore"},rel={"quest:1240","quest:1262","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={start="Bubbling Cauldron",["end"]="Nazeer Bloodpike",level="40",faction="Horde",id=1261},src={"Marg Speaks"}}
E["quest:1262"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Zor",z="dustwallow",s="Nazeer Bloodpike sends you to Orgrimmar with Marg's jeweled pendant. Strange that common soldiers carried such a fine piece, he asks Zor Lonetree, who knows Alliance politics, to judge its history.",h="Nazeer Bloodpike sends you to Orgrimmar with Marg's jeweled pendant.",sec={{t="A Noble's Pendant",b="Nazeer Bloodpike finds it strange that common soldiers carried a pendant so fine. Perhaps its owner was in disguise, or perhaps the soldiers stole it themselves. Either way, Nazeer judges it a noble's pendant. Its true owner must be found to unravel the mystery. Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar knows much of Alliance politics and can tell whether Stormwind's nobility once claimed it.",sp=0},{t="Zor's Verdict",b="Zor Lonetree admires the great skill behind the pendant. Orcs would have no use for such a jewel, he says, though many humans would. Zor will have it studied and hopes its mysteries come to light in time.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the pendant being taken to Orgrimmar?",a="Nazeer Bloodpike judges it a noble's pendant. Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar knows much of Alliance politics and can tell whether it has a history among Stormwind's nobles.",al={"why send pendant to orgrimmar","why go to orgrimmar","why see zor lonetree"}},{q="Who previously had the jeweled pendant?",a="Marg stole the pendant from soldiers at an Alliance camp near Theramore. Nazeer finds it strange that common soldiers carried it and wonders whether its owner was in disguise or the soldiers stole it.",al={"who had the pendant","where did the pendant come from"}},{q="What came before this quest?",a="Before this, Marg told you in Marg Speaks that he stole the pendant from soldiers camped near Theramore.",al={"previous quest","what quest comes before"}},{q="Where is Zor Lonetree?",a="Zor Lonetree is in Orgrimmar.",al={"zor lonetree location","where is zor lonetree"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","jeweled pendant","marg speaks","nazeer bloodpike","orgrimmar","report to zor","stormwind","zor lonetree"},rel={"npc:zor-lonetree","quest:1261","quest:7541","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:orgrimmar","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:dustwallow","topic:alliance"},m={start="Nazeer Bloodpike",["end"]="Zor Lonetree",level="40",faction="Horde",id=1262},src={"Report to Zor"}}
E["quest:1268"] = {t="quest",n="Suspicious Hoofprints",z="dustwallow",s="At the Shady Rest Inn, hoofprints lead into the marsh. Its bare frame still smokes, and the tracks fade across the soft ground. Krog at Brackenwall Village should hear of them.",h="At the Shady Rest Inn, hoofprints lead into the marsh.",sec={{t="Prints in the Mud",b="The Shady Rest Inn is a smoking frame, with hoofprints stretching away into the marsh. Some impressions show clearly, while others are nearly lost in the soft ground. You carry word of the tracks to Krog at Brackenwall Village.",sp=0},{t="Krog's Reply",b="Krog suspects the quilboar or the centaur may have burned the inn. Both have a sizeable presence in the Barrens, and either could have done it. The inn's owner also lost a woman and a pup, both killed. So Krog sends Kagoro to learn where the tracks lead.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are the hoofprints?",a="The hoofprints lead away from the Shady Rest Inn, whose bare frame still smokes, and cross the marsh's soft ground.",al={"hoofprints location","where are tracks","shady rest inn prints"}},{q="Who should hear about the hoofprints?",a="You should report the hoofprints to Krog at Brackenwall Village.",al={"who do I tell","krog location","where to report hoofprints"}},{q="How many prints are there?",a="A few hoofprints show clearly, while more rows are nearly lost in the mud.",al={"how many hoofprints","how many tracks"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","centaur","dustwallow marsh","hoofprints","kagoro","krog","quilboar","shady rest inn","suspicious hoofprints"},rel={"subzone:shady-rest-inn","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow","topic:centaur","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens"},m={start="Hoofprints",["end"]="Krog",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1268},src={"Classic quest text: Suspicious Hoofprints"}}
E["quest:1269"] = {t="quest",n="Lieutenant Paval Reethe",z="dustwallow",s="At Brackenwall Village, Krog awaits Lieutenant Paval Reethe's badge and news of the Shady Rest Inn.",h="At Brackenwall Village, Krog awaits Lieutenant Paval Reethe's badge and news of the Shady Rest Inn.",sec={{t="A Glint in the Rubble",b="Beneath rubble and brush, you find a badge marked with Theramore's sign. Ash and debris cover it, but Lieutenant Paval Reethe's name is embossed below the golden anchor. Krog waits at Brackenwall Village. He asks whether you have learned what befell the Shady Rest Inn.",sp=0},{t="What Krog Knows",b="Krog calls Paval Reethe a pathetic human who abandoned the soldiers he served with. Now Reethe hides in the woods. Krog suspects him of stealing supplies, so he sent Ogron to track him down. Others share that suspicion. Krog thinks Ogron was seen heading southeast.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is on the badge?",a="The badge bears Theramore's sign, a golden anchor over white enamel. Lieutenant Paval Reethe's name is embossed beneath it.",al={"what does the badge say","theramore guard badge markings","who owns the badge"}},{q="Who gets the badge?",a="Bring the badge to Krog at Brackenwall Village.",al={"who do i bring the badge to","where does reethe's badge go","badge turn in"}},{q="Where was the badge found?",a="You found the badge beneath rubble, caked in ash and debris. Krog asks whether you have learned what befell the Shady Rest Inn.",al={"badge location","where was reethes badge found"}}},kw={"badge","brackenwall","insignia","krog","ogron","paval","reethe","theramore"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:shady-rest-inn","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Theramore Guard Badge",["end"]="Krog",level="37",faction="Horde",id=1269},src={"Classic quest text: Lieutenant Paval Reethe"}}
E["quest:1270"] = {t="quest",n="Stinky's Escape",z="dustwallow",s="In the swamp, “Stinky” Ignatz is trapped by critters before he finds bogbean. Mebok Mizzyrix of Ratchet needs the leaves for a potion, so Ignatz asks you to free and guard him as he searches. Then find Mebok in Ratchet.",h="In the swamp, “Stinky” Ignatz is trapped by critters before he finds bogbean.",sec={{t="Surrounded in the Swamp",b="“Stinky” Ignatz is glad to meet someone who will not eat him. Mebok Mizzyrix, a goblin from Ratchet, needs bogbean leaves for a potion. Ignatz says the reason does not matter; the pay was good, and he knows the swamp. But before he found the plant, critters surrounded him. He asks you to help him escape and guard him while he searches.",sp=0},{t="Word From Mebok",b="Mebok says Ignatz returned with the herbs and told him how you helped. A friend of Stinky's is a friend of his. Before Ignatz headed south to the marsh again, he asked Mebok to give you something if you ever met.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is \"Stinky\" Ignatz?",a="“Stinky” Ignatz is searching the swamp for bogbean leaves for Mebok Mizzyrix. He says he knows the swamp, yet critters surrounded him before he found the plant.",al={"who is stinky","stinky ignatz","who is the escort guy"}},{q="Why is Ignatz gathering bogbean leaves?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix, a goblin from Ratchet, needs bogbean leaves for a potion. Ignatz says the reason does not matter; the pay was good.",al={"why bogbean","what is bogbean for","mebok bogbean"}},{q="Who is Mebok Mizzyrix?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix is a goblin from Ratchet who needs bogbean leaves to brew a potion.",al={"mebok","who is mebok mizzyrix","goblin in ratchet"}},{q="Who should you speak to afterward?",a="After helping Ignatz, find Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",al={"where does stinky go","where to turn in stinkys escape"}}},kw={"bogbean","dustwallow marsh","escort","mebok mizzyrix","ratchet","stinky ignatz"},rel={"npc:mebok-mizzyrix","subzone:ratchet","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="\"Stinky\" Ignatz",["end"]="Mebok Mizzyrix",level="37",faction="Horde",id=1270},src={"Classic quest text: Stinky's Escape"}}
E["quest:1271"] = {t="quest",n="Feast at the Blue Recluse",z="dustwallow",s="In Dustwallow Marsh, you finish your work for Morgan Stern with ... and Bugs, then return to Angus Stern at the Blue Recluse.",h="In Dustwallow Marsh, you finish your work for Morgan Stern with ...",sec={{t="Back to the Blue Recluse",b="Angus Stern is Morgan Stern's uncle. You return to Angus at the Blue Recluse after helping Morgan research recipes in Dustwallow Marsh.",sp=0},{t="What Angus Has Heard",b="Angus has heard from Morgan that you aided his research and helped one of his associates out of a tight spot. The Sterns look after their friends, and a party in your honor is about to begin.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Angus Stern?",a="Angus Stern is Morgan Stern's uncle and is connected to the Blue Recluse.",al={"angus stern","blue recluse host","who throws the feast"}},{q="How is Angus Stern connected to Morgan Stern?",a="Angus is Morgan's uncle. He sent Morgan to Theramore to gather recipes for the Blue Recluse's new bayou-themed menu.",al={"angus morgan relation","stern family","is morgan angus nephew"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="It follows ... and Bugs, the last of your work for Morgan Stern in Theramore.",al={"previous quest","what comes before feast"}}},kw={"angus stern","dustwallow marsh","feast at the blue recluse","stern family","the blue recluse","morgan stern"},rel={"quest:1258","quest:1260","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Angus Stern",["end"]="Angus Stern",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=1271},src={"Feast at the Blue Recluse"}}
E["quest:1273"] = {t="quest",n="Questioning Reethe",z="dustwallow",s="Ogron has found Reethe at last and asks you to help question him. He says Reethe hid well for a human, though the days in the swamp may have driven him mad. Afterward, you return to Krog at Brackenwall Village.",h="Ogron has found Reethe at last and asks you to help question him.",sec={{t="Ogron's Search",b="Ogron has found Reethe after a long search. By Ogron's reckoning, Reethe hid well for a human. Yet Ogron fears the days in the swamp may have left Reethe mad, and wants you beside him for answers. Once you have spoken with Reethe, you return to Krog at Brackenwall Village.",sp=0},{t="Back With Krog",b="Krog is pleased that Reethe is gone from the swamp. He scorns humans as too frail to recover from even a small arrow wound. Krog decides this strand of the mystery led nowhere. The search must turn elsewhere.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who found Reethe?",a="Ogron found Reethe after a long search and wants you beside him to get answers.",al={"who gives questioning reethe","questioning reethe quest giver","ogron reethe"}},{q="Why does Ogron want company?",a="Ogron fears Reethe may have gone mad after so long in the swamp.",al={"why help ogron","is reethe crazy","why confront reethe"}},{q="Who do you report to afterward?",a="You report to Krog at Brackenwall Village.",al={"where to turn in questioning reethe","who do i talk to after reethe","reethe turn in"}}},kw={"brackenwall","dustwallow","interrogation","krog","marsh","ogron","reethe"},rel={"quest:1269","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Ogron",["end"]="Krog",level="37",id=1273},src={"Classic quest text: Questioning Reethe"}}
E["quest:1276"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="In Thunder Bluff, Krog brings a blackened iron shield to a smith for answers. Reethe gave him nothing useful, leaving Mosarn as his only lead.",h="In Thunder Bluff, Krog brings a blackened iron shield to a smith for answers.",sec={{t="A Smith's Name",b="Krog remembers Mosarn as a highly regarded blacksmith in Thunder Bluff. The Earthen Ring once thanked Krog with armor Mosarn had crafted, and Krog speaks well of that work. He believes Mosarn made the shield too and may know more. It is a slim lead. Reethe yielded nothing useful, so Krog brings the blackened iron shield to Mosarn in Thunder Bluff.",sp=0},{t="Mosarn's Word",b="Mosarn confirms that he made the shield himself, but remembers little else. He has made so many shields and armor sets that he cannot recall them all.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Mosarn?",a="Mosarn is a highly regarded blacksmith in Thunder Bluff. He crafted the armor the Earthen Ring gave Krog.",al={"who is mosarn","where is mosarn","mosarn thunder bluff"}},{q="Why take the shield to Mosarn?",a="Krog believes Mosarn made the shield and may know more about it. Reethe yielded nothing useful, so this slim lead is all Krog has.",al={"why show mosarn the shield","blackened shield lead","what does mosarn know"}},{q="How does Krog know Mosarn?",a="The Earthen Ring thanked Krog with armor crafted by Mosarn.",al={"krog mosarn connection","how does krog know the smith"}}},kw={"blackened iron shield","blacksmith","dustwallow","earthen ring","krog","mosarn","reethe","thunder bluff"},rel={"quest:1323","zone:thunderbluff","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Krog",["end"]="Mosarn",level="37",id=1276},src={"Classic quest text: The Black Shield"}}
E["quest:1282"] = {t="quest",n="They Call Him Smiling Jim",z="dustwallow",s="Guard Byron sends you to Theramore for the story of They Call Him Smiling Jim. He hints that Jim's life was not always this way.",h="Guard Byron sends you to Theramore for the story of They Call Him Smiling Jim.",sec={{t="A Sad Story",b="Guard Byron remembers the fine inn Smiling Jim once kept in the marsh. He pities Jim, but would rather not speak of what changed. For the full story, ask Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.",sp=0},{t="Vimes's Account",b="Captain Garran Vimes says the man's name was James Hyal. Hyal built an inn on the edge of the Barrens as a pleasant stop for travelers, and it prospered for a time.\n\nThen Theramore lost its hold on the marsh roads, and ogres moved in. Hyal clung to his dream instead of seeking safety behind Theramore's walls. Fire consumed the Shady Rest Inn. The investigation has found little so far, and anyone who wants to help can search the rubble.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Smiling Jim?",a="Guard Byron pities Smiling Jim and says his life was not always this way. Jim once kept a fine inn in the marsh.",al={"who is jim","smiling jim identity","who is the smiling man"}},{q="Why does Guard Byron send you to Captain Vimes?",a="Byron would rather not discuss Jim's past, so he sends you to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.",al={"why talk to vimes","byron quest","guard byron reason"}},{q="Where do I find Captain Garran Vimes?",a="Captain Garran Vimes is in Theramore.",al={"who is captain vimes","captain vimes dustwallow"}}},kw={"captain garran vimes","dustwallow marsh","guard byron","james hyal","shady rest inn","smiling jim","theramore"},rel={"quest:1302","subzone:shady-rest-inn","zone:dustwallow","zone:barrens"},m={start="Guard Byron",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="35",id=1282},src={"Classic quest text: They Call Him Smiling Jim"}}
E["quest:1284"] = {t="quest",n="Suspicious Hoofprints",z="dustwallow",s="Smoke rises from the Shady Rest Inn, and Suspicious Hoofprints cross the marsh. Some prints are clear; others fade in the soft mud. Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore needs the report.",h="Smoke rises from the Shady Rest Inn, and Suspicious Hoofprints cross the marsh.",sec={{t="Prints in the Mud",b="Hoofprints lead from the smoking ruin of the Shady Rest Inn into the marsh. Some are easy to see, while others nearly vanish in the soft mud. Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore needs to hear about them.",sp=0},{t="What Vimes Makes of It",b="Centaur activity is common near Dustwallow Marsh. Short trips into the Barrens have revealed their camps and holdings scattered across the area. Vimes will send Falgran Hastil, one of the trackers, to learn where the prints lead.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are the hoofprints found?",a="The prints lead from the still-smoking Shady Rest Inn and across the soft marsh mud.",al={"where are the tracks","hoofprint location","shady rest inn prints"}},{q="Who receives the report about the prints?",a="Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore receives the report.",al={"who do i tell about the hoofprints","who gets the hoofprints report","garran vimes hoofprints"}},{q="How easy are the prints to follow?",a="Some prints are clear, but many nearly vanish in the mud.",al={"are the prints hard to see","faint tracks marsh"}}},kw={"barrens","captain garran vimes","centaur","dustwallow marsh","falgran hastil","hoofprints","shady rest inn","theramore"},rel={"subzone:shady-rest-inn","zone:dustwallow","topic:centaur","zone:barrens"},m={start="Hoofprints",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=1284},src={"Classic quest text: Suspicious Hoofprints"}}
E["quest:1285"] = {t="quest",n="Daelin's Men",z="dustwallow",s="Adjutant Tesoran has found Lieutenant Paval Reethe in the guard's records. They trace Reethe's service from enlistment in the Kul Tiras marines at sixteen, through promotions for distinguished service, to the Theramore guard with Lady Proudmoore's recruits. The final entry marks Reethe missing, and Captain Garran Vimes is to hear the news.",h="Adjutant Tesoran has found Lieutenant Paval Reethe in the guard's records.",sec={{t="What the Records Say",b="Captain Garran Vimes sent you to Adjutant Tesoran, who searched the books and found Lieutenant Paval Reethe. Reethe enlisted in the Kul Tiras marines at sixteen, and distinguished service brought him promotions. Later, he joined the Theramore guard with most of the recruits who sailed over with Lady Proudmoore. The record ends by listing him as missing. Vimes, in Theramore, is to hear the news.",sp=0},{t="The Captain's Reaction",b="Captain Garran Vimes takes “missing” as Tesoran's kind word for traitor. He is sure Reethe is one of the fools whose blind loyalty to Admiral Daelin makes them turn traitor. Vimes sees bitter irony in this, since the deserters accuse Theramore of betraying the Alliance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Adjutant Tesoran?",a="Adjutant Tesoran searched the guard's records for Lieutenant Paval Reethe and read out what they say.",al={"tesoran","who gives daelins men"}},{q="What do the records say about Paval Reethe?",a="Lieutenant Paval Reethe enlisted in the Kul Tiras marines at sixteen, earned promotions through distinguished service, and later joined the Theramore guard with the recruits who sailed over with Lady Proudmoore. The record ends by listing Reethe as missing.",al={"reethe backstory","reethe record","paval reethe history"}},{q="Who gets the news about Reethe?",a="Captain Garran Vimes gets the news in Theramore.",al={"why return to vimes","garran vimes reethe"}}},kw={"adjutant tesoran","daelin's men","deserters","dustwallow marsh","garran vimes","kul tiras","paval reethe","theramore"},rel={"quest:1259","quest:1286","topic:kul-tiras","topic:alliance","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Adjutant Tesoran",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="38",id=1285},src={"Classic quest text: Daelin's Men"}}
E["quest:1286"] = {t="quest",n="The Deserters",z="dustwallow",s="At Lost Point, Captain Garran Vimes questions deserters who took Theramore’s abandoned tower.",h="At Lost Point, Captain Garran Vimes questions deserters who took Theramore’s abandoned tower.",sec={{t="A Tower Taken",b="Captain Garran Vimes struggles to hold the marsh, yet his people keep several watchtowers standing. Scouts have found deserters in an abandoned tower at Lost Point, southeast of the inn. A man named Jacken leads them. Vimes asks you to learn what Jacken knows about Reethe, though the man may not give up the information easily.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to deal with the deserters?",a="Captain Garran Vimes sends you. His scouts report deserters have settled in a tower Theramore abandoned.",al={"who starts the deserters","who gives the deserters quest"}},{q="Where are the deserters hiding?",a="The deserters are hiding at Lost Point, southeast of the inn, in an abandoned tower in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"deserters location","where is lost point"}},{q="Who leads the deserters at Lost Point?",a="A man called Jacken, also known as Balos Jacken, leads the deserters. Vimes warns that Jacken may not give up information easily.",al={"who is balos jacken","deserter leader"}},{q="What does Captain Vimes want from Balos Jacken?",a="Captain Vimes wants information about Reethe from Balos Jacken and the deserters.",al={"why find jacken","what does vimes want"}}},kw={"balos jacken","captain garran vimes","deserters","dustwallow marsh","lost point","reethe","watchtower"},rel={"quest:1285","quest:1287","subzone:lost-point","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Captain Garran Vimes",["end"]="Balos Jacken",level="38",id=1286},src={"Classic quest text: The Deserters"}}
E["quest:1287"] = {t="quest",n="The Deserters",z="dustwallow",s="Reethe has been driven from the deserter band, and Balos Jacken calls him a coward. Jacken asks you to forget the meeting. Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore is waiting to hear about Reethe.",h="Reethe has been driven from the deserter band, and Balos Jacken calls him a coward.",sec={{t="Thrown Out",b="Balos Jacken says the deserters drove Reethe out for repeatedly plundering the ogres’ stores at Brackenwall Village. The band is too small to face those ogres, he says, and Reethe crossed the line once too often. They left Reethe to manage alone. In return for the answer, Jacken asks you to forget the meeting.",sp=0},{t="Back in Theramore",b="Captain Garran Vimes says Lieutenant Caldwell will be sent against the Lost Point deserters and told to find Reethe as well. Vimes judges that the marsh is neither large nor trackless enough to keep Caldwell from finding Reethe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why was Reethe thrown out of the deserter camp?",a="Jacken says Reethe kept plundering the ogres’ stores at Brackenwall Village. The deserters are too few to face them, so they left Reethe to manage alone.",al={"why did deserters exile reethe","reethe brackenwall village","why did balos kick out reethe"}},{q="Who is Balos Jacken?",a="Balos Jacken leads the Lost Point deserters. When asked about Reethe, he calls him a coward.",al={"who is balos jacken","balos jacken lore","balos jacken dustwallow"}},{q="Who wants to hear about Reethe?",a="Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore wants to hear about Reethe. Jacken hopes you will forget you ever met the deserters.",al={"where to turn in the deserters","who wants reethe information"}}},kw={"balos jacken","brackenwall village","caldwell","deserters","garran vimes","lost point","reethe","theramore"},rel={"quest:1286","subzone:lost-point","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Balos Jacken",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="38",id=1287},src={"Classic quest text: The Deserters"}}
E["quest:1288"] = {t="quest",n="Vimes's Report",z="dustwallow",s="Captain Garran Vimes praises your work as the finest he has seen from an amateur. Now you carry his report to Theramore for Lady Jaina Proudmoore.",h="Captain Garran Vimes praises your work as the finest he has seen from an amateur.",sec={{t="A Report for Lady Proudmoore",b="Lady Jaina Proudmoore asked Captain Vimes to keep her informed about a delicate situation. He has not spoken with her for some time. He planned to deliver the report later, but now sends you in his place. You may have better answers to her questions than he does.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives you the report to take to Jaina Proudmoore?",a="Captain Garran Vimes gives you his report for Lady Jaina Proudmoore in Theramore.",al={"who starts vimes's report","who gives the report","who wrote vimes report"}},{q="Why does Captain Vimes send you instead of going himself?",a="Vimes has not spoken with Lady Proudmoore for some time, so he sends you in his place. He thinks you may have better answers to her questions.",al={"why send me","why not vimes deliver it","why jaina report"}},{q="Where does the report need to go?",a="Take the report to Lady Jaina Proudmoore in Theramore.",al={"where to turn in vimes report","where is jaina proudmoore","report destination"}}},kw={"dustwallow","garran vimes","jaina proudmoore","report","theramore","vimes"},rel={"npc:jaina-proudmoore","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Captain Garran Vimes",["end"]="Lady Jaina Proudmoore",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=1288},src={"Wowpedia: Vimes's Report"}}
E["quest:1289"] = {t="quest",n="Vimes's Report",z="dustwallow",s="Lady Jaina Proudmoore has read Vimes's Report and thanks you for aiding Captain Garran Vimes's investigation. She sends you back to Vimes in Theramore to help uncover the mystery.",h="Lady Jaina Proudmoore has read Vimes's Report and thanks you for aiding Captain Garran Vimes's investigation.",sec={{t="Back to the Captain",b="Lady Jaina Proudmoore thanks you for helping Captain Vimes's investigation. His report eases her mind because the matter is in capable hands. She sends you back to him in Theramore to help uncover the mystery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you back to Captain Vimes?",a="Lady Jaina Proudmoore sends you back after reading Captain Vimes's report.",al={"who gives vimes report","jaina quest giver","who sends me to vimes"}},{q="What does Lady Jaina think of the report?",a="Lady Jaina says your help has aided the investigation, and she thanks you. Knowing the matter is in capable hands eases her mind.",al={"jaina reaction","what does jaina say about vimes report"}},{q="Where do you find Captain Garran Vimes?",a="Captain Garran Vimes is in Theramore.",al={"where is captain vimes","captain vimes location","where to turn in vimes report"}}},kw={"captain garran vimes","dustwallow marsh","investigation","lady jaina proudmoore","theramore","vimes's report"},rel={"quest:1288","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Lady Jaina Proudmoore",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=1289},src={"Wowpedia: Vimes's Report (2)"}}
E["quest:1319"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="At Theramore's smithy, Captain Garran Vimes sends a shield to a smith who may know its maker.",h="At Theramore's smithy, Captain Garran Vimes sends a shield to a smith who may know its maker.",sec={{t="A Smith Who Can Say",b="Captain Garran Vimes knows little about the shield. So he sends you to Caz Twosprocket, one of the best blacksmiths around. Caz tends the forge in Theramore's smithy and may be able to tell you more.",sp=0},{t="The Smith's Opinion",b="Caz Twosprocket examines the iron and calls it an interesting piece. Caz says it is not their work, nor the work of any smith they know on this side of the water.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to examine the shield?",a="Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore sends you to a smith who may know more about the shield.",al={"who gives the black shield","black shield quest starter","who starts the black shield"}},{q="Who is Caz Twosprocket?",a="Caz Twosprocket tends the forge in Theramore's smithy. Vimes counts Caz among the best blacksmiths around.",al={"caz twosprocket","who is the blacksmith in theramore"}},{q="What shield is shown to Caz?",a="The Blackened Iron Shield.",al={"blackened iron shield","what shield do i show caz"}}},kw={"blackened iron shield","captain garran vimes","caz twosprocket","dustwallow marsh","the black shield","theramore"},rel={"quest:1253","quest:1320","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Captain Garran Vimes",["end"]="Caz Twosprocket",level="35",id=1319},src={"Classic quest text: The Black Shield"}}
E["quest:1320"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="Caz Twosprocket studies the black shield tied to the Shady Rest Inn mystery. One detail nearly escapes notice, and Caz sends you to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore with what was found.",h="Caz Twosprocket studies the black shield tied to the Shady Rest Inn mystery.",sec={{t="A Strap Burned Away",b="A last detail nearly escapes Caz Twosprocket while looking over the black shield. The leather strap on its back has burned away, yet it seems to have been made for a large person. Caz guesses a tauren. That is all Caz can tell, so you are sent to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore with the word and Caz's apology for not being more help.",sp=0},{t="What Vimes Makes of It",b="Captain Garran Vimes finds little to go on in what Caz has learned. Still, he says he will keep it in mind. He hopes other pieces of the mystery will fall into place and show more clearly what happened.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Caz Twosprocket find out about the shield?",a="The leather strap on the shield's back has burned away, but it seems to have been made for a large person. Caz guesses a tauren.",al={"caz findings","shield clues","black shield clue"}},{q="Who should hear what Caz found?",a="Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.",al={"who do i tell about the shield","turn in black shield","where to report shield"}}},kw={"black shield","caz twosprocket","dustwallow marsh","garran vimes","shady rest inn","tauren","theramore"},rel={"subzone:shady-rest-inn","topic:tauren","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Caz Twosprocket",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=1320},src={"The Black Shield (Alliance 3)"}}
E["quest:1321"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="Krog sends you to Brackenwall Village to ask Do'gol about the Blackened Iron Shield.",h="Krog sends you to Brackenwall Village to ask Do'gol about the Blackened Iron Shield.",sec={{t="A Second Opinion",b="Krog finds nothing unusual about the Blackened Iron Shield. Still, he thinks Do'gol, the blacksmith in Brackenwall Village, may see something more. He urges you not to expect much.",sp=0},{t="Do'gol's Answer",b="Do'gol calls the shield good, strong, and heavy. But he makes shields rather than buying them, so he has no need for it. He says you should know that.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Do'gol with the shield?",a="Krog sends you to Do'gol after finding nothing unusual about the Blackened Iron Shield.",al={"who gives the black shield quest","where do i start the black shield","black shield questgiver"}},{q="Where can Do'gol be found?",a="Do'gol is the blacksmith in Brackenwall Village.",al={"dogol location","where is dogol","find dogol"}},{q="Why does Krog send you to Do'gol?",a="Krog hopes Do'gol can tell him more about the shield, though he expects little from the inspection.",al={"why visit dogol","why show the shield to the blacksmith"}}},kw={"black shield","blackened iron shield","brackenwall village","do'gol","dustwallow marsh","krog"},rel={"quest:1251","quest:1322","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Krog",["end"]="Do'gol",level="35",id=1321},src={"Classic quest text: The Black Shield"}}
E["quest:1322"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="In Brackenwall Village, Do'gol seeks venom for a shield whose writing is hidden by burned residue. Six sacs from the marsh's Darkfang spiders hold acid that can clear its rim.",h="In Brackenwall Village, Do'gol seeks venom for a shield whose writing is hidden by burned residue.",sec={{t="Cleaning the Rim",b="At Brackenwall Village, Do'gol studies the lettering around a shield's rim. Burned grime makes it hard to read, but acid can clear the residue. Darkfang spiders in the marsh carry venom fit for the work, so Do'gol asks you for six of their venom sacs.",sp=0},{t="Once the Sacs Arrive",b="Do'gol dislikes spiders too large to sit on and squash. After thanking you for the sacs, Do'gol tears them open and pours their venom onto the shield.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks for the spider venom?",a="Do'gol asks for spider venom in Brackenwall Village.",al={"who gives the black shield","dogol quest","who starts the black shield"}},{q="Why does Do'gol need venom sacs?",a="Do'gol needs acid to clear the burned residue hiding the writing on the shield's rim. Darkfang spider venom will do.",al={"why spider acid","purpose of acidic venom sacs","why clean the shield"}},{q="Where do the acidic venom sacs come from?",a="The acidic venom sacs come from Darkfang spiders living in the marsh near Brackenwall Village.",al={"which spiders have sacs","darkfang spider location","where to get acidic venom"}},{q="How many sacs does Do'gol want?",a="Do'gol wants six Acidic Venom Sacs.",al={"how many venom sacs"}}},kw={"acidic venom sacs","brackenwall village","darkfang","do'gol","dustwallow marsh","the black shield"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Do'gol",["end"]="Do'gol",level="37",id=1322},src={"Classic quest text: The Black Shield"}}
E["quest:1323"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="In Brackenwall Village, Do'gol sends you to Krog to learn a name on the shield. The writing seems to say Mosarn, but Do'gol does not know the name.",h="In Brackenwall Village, Do'gol sends you to Krog to learn a name on the shield.",sec={{t="A Name on the Rim",b="Do'gol has rubbed the shield with too much acid, yet its writing remains hard to read. The name seems to be Mosarn, but Do'gol does not know it. Krog knows many people in Brackenwall Village, so Do'gol sends you to speak with Krog.",sp=0},{t="Krog's Answer",b="Krog recognizes the name Mosarn, though cannot place it. Krog hopes it will come back to mind. Still, Krog says the name may not matter. Shields come from all sorts of places and carry no meaning.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Do'gol?",a="Do'gol is cleaning the shield with acid so its writing can be read.",al={"dogol","who gives the black shield"}},{q="What name is on the shield?",a="The writing is hard to read, but Do'gol thinks it says Mosarn. The name is unfamiliar to Do'gol.",al={"what name is on the shield","who is mosarn","shield inscription name"}},{q="Why talk to Krog about the shield?",a="Do'gol does not know who Mosarn is, but says Krog knows many people.",al={"why talk to krog","who is krog"}},{q="Where is Krog located?",a="Krog is in Brackenwall Village.",al={"krog location","where do i find krog"}}},kw={"acid","black shield","brackenwall village","do'gol","dustwallow marsh","krog","mosarn"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Do'gol",["end"]="Krog",level="37",id=1323},src={"Classic quest text: The Black Shield"}}
E["quest:7541"] = {t="quest",n="Service to the Horde",z="dustwallow",s="In Orgrimmar, Zor Lonetree has received the jeweled pendant and has more to tell you about your service to the Horde.",h="In Orgrimmar, Zor Lonetree has received the jeweled pendant and has more to tell you about your service to...",sec={{t="Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar",b="The jeweled pendant now rests with Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar. Return to him to hear more about your service to the Horde.",sp=0},{t="Zor's Last Word",b="Zor says the scholars need time to study the pendant. He offers you a small token in recognition of your service to the Horde. Your deeds bring honor to you and to the Horde.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who has the pendant now?",a="Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar has the pendant. You brought it there from Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.",al={"who takes the pendant","who gives this quest","zor lonetree role"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="Report to Zor comes first. You brought the jeweled pendant to Zor Lonetree.",al={"what quest came before","service to the horde prerequisite","previous quest"}}},kw={"dustwallow marsh","pendant","report to zor","service to the horde","zor lonetree"},rel={"npc:zor-lonetree","quest:1262","topic:horde","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Zor Lonetree",["end"]="Zor Lonetree",level="40",faction="Horde",id=7541},src={"Service to the Horde"}}
E["subzone:beezil-s-wreck"] = {t="subzone",n="Beezil's Wreck",z="dustwallow",s="East of Tabetha's Farm, Beezil's Wreck draws scavengers to its broken zeppelin and scattered cargo.",h="East of Tabetha's Farm, Beezil's Wreck draws scavengers to its broken zeppelin and scattered cargo.",sec={{t="A Calamitous Landing",b="East of Tabetha's Farm, the goblin zeppelin lies split apart in the muck. It carried cargo south across Kalimdor before plunging into the swamp. Captain Beezil is gone from the marsh. Crates and ticking machinery lie among the reeds, rotting in the brine.",sp=0},{t="Salvage in the Muck",b="Beasts prowl around the crash site, but scavengers still brave them for the cargo that survived. The zeppelin carried volatile goods, including Seaforium boosters and heavy crates. They risk their lives to salvage what remains before marsh water corrodes it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Beezil's Wreck?",a="Beezil's Wreck lies deep in Dustwallow Marsh, east of Tabetha's Farm, where a goblin zeppelin crashed. It went down while carrying cargo south across Kalimdor.",al={"beezils wreck","crashed zeppelin dustwallow","what is this wreck"}},{q="Where is the pilot, Beezil?",a="Beezil is nowhere around the crash site. Searchers do not know whether he escaped into the wilderness or left the marsh.",al={"where is beezil","who is beezil","beezil location"}},{q="What valuable cargo was the zeppelin carrying?",a="The zeppelin carried trade goods and volatile goblin engineering components, including Seaforium boosters. Scavengers seek what survived the crash.",al={"what was in the zeppelin","seaforium boosters","wreck cargo"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can find volatile mechanical parts in the wreck, especially Seaforium boosters any tinkerer would covet.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you see the smoking goblin wreck as a grim reminder of the dangers of non-gnomish aerial design."},kw={"beezil","beezil's wreck","dustwallow marsh","seaforium","tabetha","zeppelin crash"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:tabetha-s-farm","npc:tabetha","topic:goblin"},src={"Beezil's Wreck"}}
E["subzone:bloodfen-burrow"] = {t="subzone",n="Bloodfen Burrow",z="dustwallow",s="Bloodfen raptors now crowd the cavern and clearing in southwestern Dustwallow Marsh. They have overrun the ruins of a settlement that once struggled to survive the wetlands.",h="Bloodfen raptors now crowd the cavern and clearing in southwestern Dustwallow Marsh.",sec={{t="A Den of Predators",b="Bloodfen raptors crowd the cave and hollow in southwestern Dustwallow Marsh. The sheltered crevice and rich hunting grounds draw the pack. Outside the entrance, scattered debris and splintered remains mark an unidentified settlement. Travelers also whisper that Cortello, an adventurous buccaneer, left one of his hidden riddle clues somewhere in the den.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What lives in Bloodfen Burrow?",a="Bloodfen raptors overrun the cave and surrounding clearing. Their nesting ground is dense, and they attack anyone who enters their territory.",al={"who lives here","bloodfen burrow raptors","what mobs in bloodfen burrow"}},{q="What are the ruins outside the cave?",a="The ruins outside the cave are all that remains of an unidentified settlement. Raptors destroyed it, and no record names its occupants or tells what became of them.",al={"ruined settlement dustwallow","who built the huts near bloodfen burrow","ruins outside cave"}},{q="Why would an adventurer search Bloodfen Burrow?",a="Explorers seeking Cortello's Riddle must enter Bloodfen Burrow to find one of the buccaneer's hidden clues. Fierce marsh raptors draw hunters to the cavern as well.",al={"cortello's riddle bloodfen","treasure in bloodfen burrow","bloodfen burrow quest"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you may find fierce, quick Bloodfen raptors here. They make durable, aggressive swamp companions."},kw={"bloodfen burrow","bloodfen raptor","cortello's riddle","dustwallow marsh","raptor cave"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},src={"Bloodfen Burrow"}}
E["subzone:bluefen"] = {t="subzone",n="Bluefen",z="dustwallow",s="Bluefen’s marsh paths put travelers between swamp predators and Theramore scouts. The bog lies in northern Dustwallow Marsh, just east of Brackenwall Village.",h="Bluefen’s marsh paths put travelers between swamp predators and Theramore scouts.",sec={{t="A Contested Bog",b="East of Brackenwall Village, home to the Stonemaul ogres, Bluefen’s wet ground teems with danger. Raptors, giant spiders, carrion-feeding birds, and crocolisks prowl the marsh. Theramore Infiltrators also move through the bog, watching Horde movements and carrying human influence deeper into the swamp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Bluefen located?",a="Bluefen lies in northern Dustwallow Marsh, just east of Brackenwall Village.",al={"bluefen location","where is bluefen","bluefen map"}},{q="What threats can be found in Bluefen?",a="Raptors, giant spiders, crocolisks, and carrion-feeding birds hunt in Bluefen. Theramore Infiltrators also scout the marsh and threaten Horde travelers.",al={"bluefen enemies","what lives in bluefen","bluefen mobs"}},{q="Why are Theramore scouts active in Bluefen?",a="Theramore Infiltrators watch Brackenwall Village, home to the Stonemaul ogres, and patrol the contested paths through northern Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"theramore infiltrators","why are alliance here","theramore spies"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="East of Brackenwall Village, Bluefen puts Horde champions among swamp beasts and Theramore Infiltrators watching the Stonemaul ogres.",["faction:Alliance"]="Wild beasts make travel treacherous, while Theramore scouts watch the nearby ogre encampment through Bluefen’s dense marsh foliage."},kw={"bluefen","brackenwall","crocolisks","dustwallow","marsh","theramore infiltrators"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:brackenwall-village"},src={"Bluefen"}}
E["subzone:brackenwall-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Brackenwall Village",z="dustwallow",s="In the northwest marsh, Brackenwall Village shelters the Stonemaul ogres. Black dragonkin drove them from their southern home, and spies, deserters, and the black dragonflight now threaten the refuge.",h="In the northwest marsh, Brackenwall Village shelters the Stonemaul ogres.",sec={{t="Refuge of the Stonemaul",b="Overlord Mok'Morokk led the Stonemaul survivors north after black dragonkin drove them from their ancient home at Stonemaul Village. Successor to Rexxar, he gathered the clan in the swamp to build Brackenwall. Earthen mounds, huts, and an old watchtower give the battered ogres a refuge they can defend.\n\nBrackenwall is allied with the Horde, but Mok'Morokk sits idle, hoards supplies, and refuses to face the draconic threat. The ogre mage Draz'Zilb and Horde emissaries give the clan spiritual and tactical guidance.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Bog",b="Theramore infiltrators watch Brackenwall from the thickets and report the village's movements to the island fortress. Paval Reethe, a Theramore deserter cast out from Lost Point, is suspected of stealing vital supplies from the outpost.\n\nWary eyes watch from the east as black drakes prowl the southern reaches. Brackenwall remains an isolated Horde staging ground against the Alliance and Onyxia's brood.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are there ogres allied with the Horde here?",a="The Stonemaul ogres joined the modern Horde through Rexxar, their champion during the founding of Durotar. After defeating their former leader, Rexxar became their chieftain and bound the clan to Warchief Thrall's coalition. He later passed leadership to Mok'Morokk.",al={"why horde ogres","stonemaul clan lore","who are these ogres"}},{q="Why did the Stonemaul settle here instead of staying in their old home?",a="Black dragonkin overran and destroyed the Stonemaul's ancestral settlement in southern Dustwallow Marsh. Overlord Mok'Morokk led the displaced survivors north through the bog to build Brackenwall as a fortified refuge.",al={"what happened to stonemaul village","why brackenwall","ogre refugees"}},{q="Who is in charge of Brackenwall Village?",a="Overlord Mok'Morokk leads Brackenwall, though many resent his rule. He cowers in the village instead of rallying the ogres to reclaim their homeland or confront the dragons. The ogre mage Draz'Zilb and Horde envoys manage daily crises.",al={"brackenwall leader","who runs brackenwall","mok'morokk"}},{q="Why are there Theramore spies outside the village?",a="Theramore's military watches Horde troop movements in Dustwallow despite the fragile truce between Theramore and Orgrimmar. Infiltrators circle Brackenwall and report on ogre strength and Horde operations.",al={"alliance spies dustwallow","theramore infiltrators","why is theramore watching"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Brackenwall is your only sanctuary and flight connection in the marsh. Defending it helps the Horde keep a vital listening post and defensive flank against Theramore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Brackenwall lies deep in hostile territory. Investigations into the missing diplomat and rogue Theramore deserters will bring daring agents to the edge of the ogre encampment."},kw={"brackenwall","draz'zilb","dustwallow","infiltrators","mok'morokk","ogres","paval reethe","stonemaul"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","npc:overlord-mok-morokk","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","topic:horde","npc:onyxia","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:lost-point","quest:1241"},src={"Brackenwall Village"}}
E["subzone:darkmist-cavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkmist Cavern",z="dustwallow",s="Darkmist spiders swarm the old mine in northwestern Dustwallow Marsh. Ruined shacks stand by its entrance, and locals still dispute whether cave or brood bore the name first.",h="Darkmist spiders swarm the old mine in northwestern Dustwallow Marsh.",sec={{t="The Brood in the Mine",b="Rotting shacks stand outside Darkmist Cavern in northwestern Dustwallow Marsh. Thick webs choke the tunnels. People once came here for the mine, but no human presence remains. Now Darkmist spiders fill its passages. Their size and venom make them deadly to unwary wanderers.\n\nMarsh dwellers still dispute how the cavern got its name. Some say it was named for the brood nesting inside. Others say the spiders took their name from the misty cave.",sp=0},{t="Hermit's Larder",b="Even this web choked cavern draws scavengers. The hermit ‘Swamp Eye’ Jarl sends travelers deep into its webs to gather the eyes of monstrous spiders. He claims they make fine broth. Most sensible travelers keep clear of the web strewn entrance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Darkmist Cavern?",a="Darkmist Cavern is an abandoned mine in northwestern Dustwallow Marsh, now filled with giant, venomous Darkmist spiders.",al={"what is darkmist cavern","darkmist cave","spider cave dustwallow"}},{q="Who lived at the ruins outside the cave?",a="The ruins outside the cave suggest a settlement or mining camp once stood there, but no one knows who lived there.",al={"who lived here","houses outside darkmist cavern","abandoned village darkmist"}},{q="Why do locals venture into Darkmist Cavern?",a="Few willingly enter Darkmist Cavern. The hermit ‘Swamp Eye’ Jarl sends daring travelers into its tunnels to retrieve spider eyes for his strange marsh stew.",al={"why go to darkmist cavern","darkmist cavern quest"}},{q="Did the spiders or the cavern get the name first?",a="Dustwallow Marsh’s inhabitants disagree over whether the cavern was named for the spiders or the spiders for the cavern. No settled account says which name came first.",al={"spider name origin","why is it called darkmist"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="The hermit ‘Swamp Eye’ Jarl calls Darkmist spider eyes the finest ingredient for marsh stew. Few beyond the swamp share his taste.",["profession:Mining"]="Miners once hollowed out the cavern. Anyone hoping to prospect its rocky depths must first face the nesting spiders."},kw={"darkmist cavern","darkmist spiders","dustwallow marsh","mine ruins","spider mine","swamp eye jarl"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},src={"Darkmist Cavern"}}
E["subzone:den-of-flame"] = {t="subzone",n="Den of Flame",z="dustwallow",s="Black dragonkin hold the Den of Flame in western Dustwallow Marsh, west of the Stonemaul Ruins. The Stonemaul ogres raised it as their mound, but Onyxia’s brood has driven them out.",h="Black dragonkin hold the Den of Flame in western Dustwallow Marsh, west of the Stonemaul Ruins.",sec={{t="A Conquered Mound",b="Black dragonspawn patrol the burning edge of the Den of Flame and guard its cavern entrance. The Stonemaul ogres built the rough stone stronghold as their main mound and sanctuary. Then the black dragonflight laid waste to the clan’s settlement. The brood scattered the ogres and seized the mound, where dragonspawn now keep watch beneath the shadow of Onyxia’s nearby lair.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Den of Flame originally built for?",a="The Stonemaul ogres built the Den of Flame as their clan’s main mound. Its stonework and layout follow ogre clan architecture.",al={"who built den of flame","den of flame origin","ogre mound dustwallow"}},{q="Why are black dragonkin infesting this mound?",a="Onyxia established her lair nearby in the marsh. Her dragonkin drove the Stonemaul ogres from their settlement and claimed the cavern as a forward outpost for the brood.",al={"why are there dragons here","who lives in den of flame","dragonspawn dustwallow"}},{q="Can the Stonemaul ogres reclaim the cave?",a="Not for now. The surviving Stonemaul ogres have settled at Brackenwall Village alongside the Horde. Black dragonspawn hold their old mound in force.",al={"reclaiming the den"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Stonemaul ogres are sworn allies of the Horde. Clearing dragonkin from the Den of Flame helps avenge their fallen settlement."},kw={"black dragonflight","den of flame","dragonspawn","dustwallow marsh","onyxia","stonemaul ruins"},rel={"subzone:stonemaul-ruins","npc:onyxia","topic:black-dragonflight","zone:dustwallow"},src={"Den of Flame"}}
E["subzone:dragonmurk"] = {t="subzone",n="Dragonmurk",z="dustwallow",s="In southern Dustwallow Marsh, black dragonspawn and hatchlings swarm Dragonmurk. Ancient ogre ruins and scorched caverns flank this dangerous tract, held by Onyxia's brood.",h="In southern Dustwallow Marsh, black dragonspawn and hatchlings swarm Dragonmurk.",sec={{t="A Brood in the Bog",b="In southern Dustwallow Marsh, wet paths and thick mud teem with black wyrmkins, dragonspawn, and hungry whelps. The black dragonflight holds the land around Dragonmurk. Stonemaul, a ruined village, and the scorched Den of Flame both lie under its control.",sp=0},{t="Guarding the Broodmother",b="Onyxia's black dragonspawn fill the mire, guarding her clutch. Southern Dustwallow is Onyxia's main nesting ground in Kalimdor. She is the daughter of Deathwing. Her wyrmkin patrol the marsh and destroy intruders, protecting the eggs from Theramore's scouts and nearby Horde camps.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Dragonmurk?",a="Dragonmurk is a southern stretch of Dustwallow Marsh overrun by black dragonflight whelps, drakes, and dragonspawn.",al={"what is dragonmurk","where is dragonmurk","dragonmurk location"}},{q="Why are there so many black dragons here?",a="Onyxia's lair lies in southern Dustwallow Marsh, where her offspring and servants nest, grow, and keep outside threats at bay.",al={"why black dragons in dustwallow","who leads the dragons here","onyxia dragons dustwallow"}},{q="What landmarks are found near Dragonmurk?",a="The Den of Flame and the Stonemaul Ruins lie in and around Dragonmurk. Black dragonspawn occupy both.",al={"dragonmurk landmarks","what is near dragonmurk","places around dragonmurk"}},{q="Is Dragonmurk safe for travelers?",a="No. Hostile, aggressive dragonkin make Dragonmurk one of southern Kalimdor's most perilous wilderness regions.",al={"is dragonmurk dangerous","can i walk through dragonmurk"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Black dragons drove the Stonemaul ogres from their village. They still threaten Horde expeditions that venture deep into the marsh.",["faction:Alliance"]="Theramore watches Dragonmurk closely. An unchecked black dragon brood so near the fortress could spell disaster."},kw={"black dragonflight","den of flame","dragonmurk","dragonspawn","dustwallow marsh","onyxia","stonemaul ruins","whelps"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","topic:black-dragonflight","subzone:den-of-flame","subzone:stonemaul-ruins"},src={"Dragonmurk"}}
E["subzone:dreadmurk-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Dreadmurk Shore",z="dustwallow",s="Fog and Mirefin murlocs endanger travelers on Dreadmurk Shore, between Theramore Isle and the Barrens. Sea beasts prowl the water, making this coast a dangerous passage through Dustwallow Marsh.",h="Fog and Mirefin murlocs endanger travelers on Dreadmurk Shore, between Theramore Isle and the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Treacherous Coast",b="At Dustwallow Marsh’s northeastern edge, muddy shoals, tide pools, and misty islands lie between Theramore Isle and Northwatch Hold. The Mirefin tribe holds this coast. These territorial murlocs attack travelers who come near their villages. Sea turtles and other aquatic predators patrol the shallows, while the swamplands bring danger from inland.",sp=0},{t="Defias Infiltrators",b="A Defias Brotherhood ship wrecked between Dreadmurk Shore and Alcaz Island. Outlaws spilled onto the sand and islets. These human criminals came from the Eastern Kingdoms and now lie close to Lady Jaina Proudmoore’s stronghold. Their presence draws Theramore’s attention and threatens the fragile balance of power across the bay.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Dreadmurk Shore located?",a="Dreadmurk Shore runs along Dustwallow Marsh’s northeastern coast, facing the Great Sea between Theramore Isle and the Barrens, near Northwatch Hold.",al={"dreadmurk shore location","where is dreadmurk shore"}},{q="Why are there Defias bandits on this shore?",a="A Defias Brotherhood ship recently wrecked offshore between Dreadmurk Shore and Alcaz Island. Survivors reached the isolated beach and outcroppings, where they made temporary camps and tried to salvage their sunken cargo.",al={"defias in dustwallow","why are defias here","shipwrecked defias"}},{q="Who are the murlocs living along the beach?",a="The Mirefin murloc tribe lives along the coast. Its members built crude fishing settlements on the sandbanks and rocky islets, and fiercely guard their territory from Theramore patrols and shipwrecked intruders.",al={"mirefin murlocs","dreadmurk shore murlocs"}},{q="Is Dreadmurk Shore controlled by Theramore?",a="Theramore claims authority over the lands around the island, but Dreadmurk Shore remains lawless. Wild marshy shoals and murloc and brigand inhabitants keep Lady Jaina Proudmoore’s sentries from regular patrols.",al={"who owns dreadmurk shore","is dreadmurk shore alliance"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Defias Brotherhood survivors near Theramore suggest conspiracies reaching beyond Westfall. They threaten Alliance stability in Kalimdor.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can track clandestine Defias cargo through isolated camps and sunken wreckage. Or you can slip past the violent Mirefin sentinels."},kw={"alcaz island","defias","dreadmurk shore","dustwallow marsh","mirefin","murloc","shipwreck","theramore"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:theramore-isle","topic:murloc","zone:barrens"},src={"Dreadmurk Shore"}}
E["subzone:dustwallow-bay"] = {t="subzone",n="Dustwallow Bay",z="dustwallow",s="Vessels thread the shallow waters of Dustwallow Bay on their way to Theramore Isle. The inlet lies between Dustwallow Marsh and the island, with coves and shoals far from eastern Kalimdor’s main sea routes.",h="Vessels thread the shallow waters of Dustwallow Bay on their way to Theramore Isle.",sec={{t="Waters of the Eastern Marsh",b="At Dustwallow Marsh, murky wetlands meet the Great Sea. Theramore Isle lies to the east, and ships cross the bay to reach Lady Jaina Proudmoore’s island haven. Vessels come and go from its docks, though the coast remains wild and dangerous. Rocky outcrops, murloc encampments, and hidden inlets such as Tidefury Cove line the shore.",sp=0},{t="A Fisherman's Haven",b="Beyond the marsh’s crocolisks and hostile beasts, the islands and inlets offer quiet waters and rich catches. Small islets near Tidefury Cove draw anglers seeking solitude. Nat Pagle, the famed fisherman, often casts from the rocks, away from Theramore’s crowds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Dustwallow Bay located?",a="Dustwallow Bay runs along the eastern coast of central Kalimdor, between the sodden eastern shores of Dustwallow Marsh and Theramore Isle.",al={"dustwallow bay location","where is dustwallow bay","dustwallow water"}},{q="Who can be found in the bay?",a="Nat Pagle, the famed angler, can be found in the bay’s outer reaches. He camps on a small islet in nearby Tidefury Cove, southwest of Theramore Isle.",al={"who is in dustwallow bay","nat pagle dustwallow bay","npcs dustwallow bay"}},{q="Is Dustwallow Bay safe to swim across?",a="Swimming across the bay is dangerous. Murlocs, sharks, and other aggressive aquatic wildlife frequent its shallows and coasts.",al={"is dustwallow bay dangerous","monsters in dustwallow bay"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance sailors and travelers bound for Kalimdor, Dustwallow Bay is the last stretch of open sea before Theramore Isle’s fortified harbor."},kw={"dustwallow bay","dustwallow marsh","great sea","nat pagle","theramore","tidefury cove"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:tidefury-cove","npc:nat-pagle"},src={"Dustwallow Bay"}}
E["subzone:foothold-citadel"] = {t="subzone",n="Foothold Citadel",z="dustwallow",s="At Foothold Citadel, Theramore's guards prepare to defend the island. The fortress holds the Alliance command and barracks on Theramore Isle, overlooking the settlement.",h="At Foothold Citadel, Theramore's guards prepare to defend the island.",sec={{t="Heart of the Theramore Guard",b="Foothold Citadel holds the Alliance defense within Theramore Isle's stone walls. Captain Garran Vimes and Commander Samaul lead the Theramore Guard from its halls. Field medics, logistics officers and quartermasters work beside them. Guards patrol and drill, preparing Lady Jaina Proudmoore's forces for threats from the surrounding swamplands.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Admiral's Fall",b="Foothold Citadel recalls the early days of Theramore. Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore seized the city to wage his personal crusade against the Horde, and the fortress became the place of his final stand. Thrall's allied force broke through the citadel under Rexxar, a half-ogre warrior, and struck down the Admiral. The fortress has been repaired, though the bloody conflict is remembered.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Foothold Citadel used for?",a="Foothold Citadel is the Theramore Guard's headquarters and barracks. Command officers, tactical planners, training facilities and logistics staff work there, along with the local paymaster and medical personnel.",al={"foothold citadel purpose","theramore barracks","what is this building"}},{q="What happened to Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore here?",a="During the conflict after the Third War, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore seized Theramore to wage war on the young Horde. A combined force led by the champion Rexxar stormed the citadel and killed the Admiral in his own headquarters.",al={"daelin death","daelin proudmoore last stand","who killed daelin"}},{q="Who is currently in charge at Foothold Citadel?",a="Captain Garran Vimes and Commander Samaul oversee the garrison's daily patrols and regional security under Lady Jaina Proudmoore's authority.",al={"who leads the citadel","theramore guard commander","citadel leader"}},{q="Can I receive medical aid inside the citadel?",a="Yes. Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen lives inside Foothold Citadel. He tends wounded guardsmen and teaches Alliance travelers advanced field medicine and triage.",al={"citadel doctor","theramore medic","first aid trainer theramore"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Foothold Citadel is the Alliance's main military post in southern Kalimdor. Its officers coordinate defense against swamp beasts, Grimtotem marauders and watchful Horde scouts.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde remembers Foothold Citadel as the place where Rexxar and Thrall ended Grand Admiral Proudmoore's campaign to protect Durotar."},kw={"barracks","daelin proudmoore","dustwallow marsh","foothold citadel","garran vimes","gustaf vanhowzen","samaul","theramore"},rel={"subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","topic:alliance","npc:doctor-gustaf-vanhowzen","npc:thrall"},src={"Foothold Citadel"}}
E["subzone:lost-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Lost Point",z="dustwallow",s="At Lost Point in western Dustwallow, deserters have driven out Lady Jaina Proudmoore's guard. Theramore built the tower as an advance scout post, but it has fallen into disrepair.",h="At Lost Point in western Dustwallow, deserters have driven out Lady Jaina Proudmoore's guard.",sec={{t="A Forsaken Outpost",b="Lost Point once watched the Barrens for traffic and threats on Theramore's behalf. Its military purpose passed, and marsh damp rotted the timber. Regular troops abandoned the defenses. Now human deserters from Theramore hold the tower and the nearby ground. They found shelter in this isolated wilderness, far from the discipline of the city's commanders.",sp=0},{t="Den of Deserters",b="Balos Jacken leads the deserters at Lost Point. A disgruntled former soldier, Jacken holds key testimony with his followers about traitorous elements within Theramore's ranks. Their testimony includes Private Hendel's part in a conspiracy that reaches into the Alliance's upper ranks.",sp=1,bt={"q1274.5"}}},faq={{q="What is Lost Point?",a="Lost Point is a rundown watchtower in western Dustwallow, built by Theramore's humans as an advance scout post. The military abandoned it, and deserters now occupy it.",al={"lost point overview","what is this tower","about lost point"}},{q="Who lives at Lost Point right now?",a="Theramore deserters live in the tower and the camp around it. These human soldiers abandoned their oaths and follow Balos Jacken.",al={"who is at lost point","lost point enemies","lost point mobs"}},{q="Who is Balos Jacken?",a="Balos Jacken leads the Theramore deserters hiding at Lost Point. He holds crucial intelligence about troubling matters in Theramore's ranks.",al={"balos jacken","deserter leader","who leads lost point"},sp=1},{q="Why did Theramore abandon the tower?",a="Dustwallow Marsh is hostile and difficult to supply. As morale fell and discipline frayed among the garrison, the isolated tower decayed. It became shelter for soldiers escaping duty without fleeing into Horde territory.",al={"why abandoned","why is lost point ruined","why run down"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance loyalist, Lost Point is a bitter sign of fraying discipline in Theramore's ranks. Renegades there hold key testimonies about military treason."},kw={"balos jacken","dustwallow marsh","lost point","scout tower","theramore deserters"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},src={"Lost Point"}}
E["subzone:nat-s-landing"] = {t="subzone",n="Nat's Landing",z="dustwallow",s="At Nat's Landing, fishermen come to Dustwallow Bay seeking Nat Pagle's highest instruction. The famous angler keeps a quiet camp there.",h="At Nat's Landing, fishermen come to Dustwallow Bay seeking Nat Pagle's highest instruction.",sec={{t="A Master's Haven",b="Southwest of Theramore Isle, you find Nat's Landing beside the murky waters of Dustwallow Bay. A canvas tent, drying racks for the day's catch, spare tackle in the trees, and a rickety pier mark the weathered camp. Mists and swamp dangers surround this quiet shore. Nat Pagle comes here for solitude and a drink, away from the clamor of civilization.",sp=0},{t="The Fisherman's Pilgrimage",b="Anglers who have learned all they can from trainers in Ironforge, Orgrimmar, and elsewhere are sent to Nat Pagle. Politics and factional quarrels mean nothing to him. To earn his highest instruction, you must brave marshland predators and show patience and skill across the world's most perilous waters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Nat's Landing located?",a="Nat's Landing lies along Dustwallow Bay in eastern Dustwallow Marsh, southwest of Theramore Isle.",al={"where is nats landing","nats landing location","how to get to nats landing"}},{q="Who lives at Nat's Landing?",a="Nat Pagle, the renowned human angler, keeps his personal campsite at Nat's Landing.",al={"who is at nats landing","nats landing npc","who lives here"}},{q="Why do anglers travel here?",a="Fishermen who have learned all they can from local trainers travel to Nat Pagle. He tests their dedication with challenging catches around the world before teaching them at the highest level.",al={"why come to nats landing","artisan fishing trainer","nat pagle training"}},{q="Does Nat Pagle welcome both Alliance and Horde?",a="Yes. Nat Pagle welcomes dedicated anglers from either faction, regardless of their loyalties.",al={"is nats landing hostile","can horde talk to nat","is nat pagle neutral"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance citizen stationed in Theramore, you can walk a short, quiet way down the coast to Nat's Landing and reach the world's premier fisherman.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde angler crossing the perilous swamp from the Barrens, you will find Nat indifferent to the war. He judges visitors by the quality of their cast."},kw={"angler","dock","dustwallow bay","dustwallow marsh","fishing","nat pagle","nats landing","theramore"},rel={"npc:nat-pagle","zone:dustwallow","subzone:dustwallow-bay","quest:6608","subzone:zul-gurub","zone:ironforge","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Nat's Landing"}}
E["subzone:onyxia-s-lair"] = {t="subzone",n="Onyxia's Lair",z="dustwallow",s="Deep in the Wyrmbog, magma burns beneath the marsh in Onyxia's Lair. Onyxia keeps her stronghold and nesting place here, watching over clutches of black dragon eggs.",h="Deep in the Wyrmbog, magma burns beneath the marsh in Onyxia's Lair.",sec={{t="A Den of Magma and Ruin",b="The entrance cuts through the Wyrmbog's mud and petrified wood like a dragon's open maw. Beyond it, volcanic heat drives out the marsh's cool rot. Magma seeps through cracks in the obsidian, and tremors often shake the ceilings. In a vast chamber, hundreds of black dragon eggs lie among ash and embers. Flightkin and dragonspawn guards watch the clutch beside Onyxia.",sp=0},{t="The Broodmother's Retreat",b="Onyxia keeps a secluded roost on Kalimdor to breed the next generation of the black dragonflight. Across the sea, her brother Nefarian plots from Blackrock Spire. When her political schemes unravel, the lair offers refuge. Far from mortal courts, Onyxia can cast off her human guises and take her true form as Deathwing's daughter.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where exactly is Onyxia's Lair?",a="Onyxia's Lair lies in southern Dustwallow Marsh, within the Wyrmbog just south of the Dragonmurk. Massive dragon bones and smoldering ground mark the entrance, where black dragonkin guard a stony fissure shaped like an open jaw.",al={"where is onyxia","onyxia location","how to find onyxia lair","dragonmurk cave"}},{q="What creatures dwell inside the lair?",a="Members of the black dragonflight dwell in the cavern. Broodmother Onyxia commands its deep chamber among freshly hatched whelps, guardian dragonspawn, and mature black drakes.",al={"onyxia lair mobs","who lives in onyxia lair","what is inside"}},{q="Why is the cave so hot if it sits in a swamp?",a="Onyxia dug deep into Kalimdor's crust and reached subterranean veins of magma. The volcanic heat incubates black dragon eggs, while cold mud covers the marsh above.",al={"why is there lava in dustwallow","onyxia lair volcano"}},{q="Why is Onyxia hiding out in Kalimdor?",a="Dustwallow Marsh gives Onyxia isolation and concealment. Thick fogs, dismal quagmires, and dangerous wildlife keep mortal armies away, letting her replenish her flight undisturbed as she meddles abroad.",al={"why is onyxia here","why dustwallow marsh","onyxia kalimdor"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions, this cavern is the den of a black broodmother whose growing brood threatens Theramore and every settlement around the marsh.",["faction:Horde"]="Dustwallow Marsh borders Horde territory in the Barrens and Mulgore. A black broodmother hatching an army of dragons on Kalimdor threatens the whole new Horde."},kw={"black dragonflight","broodmother","dragonmurk","dustwallow","lair","onyxia","whelps","wyrmbog"},rel={"npc:onyxia","subzone:dragonmurk","zone:dustwallow","topic:black-dragonflight","subzone:wyrmbog","npc:deathwing","zone:stormwind"},src={"Onyxia's Lair"}}
E["subzone:quagmire"] = {t="subzone",n="Quagmire",z="dustwallow",s="In central Dustwallow Marsh, the Quagmire is a perilous stretch of fen. Brackenwall Village lies north and the Dragonmurk south. Waterlogged flats, hostile beasts, and ravenous oozes make crossing it dangerous.",h="In central Dustwallow Marsh, the Quagmire is a perilous stretch of fen.",sec={{t="Heart of the Fen",b="The Quagmire runs from Lost Point in the west to Dustwallow Bay in the east, through the marsh’s wild heart. Solid ground can give way to murky water and clinging mud without warning. Crocolisks wait beneath the scum, aggressive spiders nest in dead brush, and strange oozes seep through the muck.",sp=0},{t="Encroaching Clashes",b="The Quagmire lies where sentient powers contest the swamp, an unpredictable crossing in their struggles. Tabetha's Farm stands in the bog as a lonely refuge. There, practitioners seek wisdom from a hermit amid the swamp’s dangers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Quagmire located?",a="The Quagmire covers central Dustwallow Marsh, from Lost Point in the west to Dustwallow Bay in the east. Brackenwall Village lies north, while the land descends into the Dragonmurk to the south.",al={"quagmire location","where is the quagmire","quagmire map"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Deep in the fen, Tabetha's Farm draws aspiring mages seeking esoteric training beyond the Kirin Tor's scrutiny."},kw={"beezil","crocolisk","dustwallow","quagmire","tabetha"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:dragonmurk","subzone:tabetha-s-farm","subzone:beezil-s-wreck","subzone:lost-point","topic:tauren"},src={"Quagmire"}}
E["subzone:sentry-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Sentry Point",z="dustwallow",s="At Sentry Point, Theramore's forces watch the causeway to their island citadel. From the mainland edge of Dustwallow Marsh, the human watchtower overlooks traffic in both directions.",h="At Sentry Point, Theramore's forces watch the causeway to their island citadel.",sec={{t="The Gates of Theramore",b="Sentry Point guards the western end of the bridge between Theramore Isle and Dustwallow Marsh. From its stone scout tower, Theramore's forces watch the swamp road. They guard the mainland approach to the island city and watch for marsh beasts and Horde raiders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Sentry Point used for?",a="Sentry Point warns Theramore Isle of approaching threats and checks traffic on the swamp road. Its guards watch travelers and alert the city guards when danger nears.",al={"sentry point purpose","what is this tower","why is sentry point here"}},{q="Who controls this outpost?",a="Theramore's forces man and maintain Sentry Point under Lady Jaina Proudmoore and her military officers.",al={"who owns sentry point","is sentry point alliance","theramore guard tower"}},{q="Is Sentry Point safe for Horde travelers?",a="No. Lady Jaina Proudmoore seeks peace with the Horde, but Sentry Point's guards protect Alliance territory and attack Horde travelers who trespass.",al={"can horde go to sentry point","horde friendly sentry point"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For travelers crossing Dustwallow Marsh's dangerous bogs, Sentry Point marks the welcoming threshold to the safety of Theramore Isle.",["faction:Horde"]="Sentry Point's guarded tower makes Theramore's military presence on the Kalimdor mainland plain to approaching Horde scouts."},kw={"bridge","dustwallow marsh","guard tower","jaina proudmoore","sentry point","theramore","watchtower"},rel={"subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","npc:jaina-proudmoore"},src={"Sentry Point"}}
E["subzone:shady-rest-inn"] = {t="subzone",n="Shady Rest Inn",z="dustwallow",s="At the Shady Rest Inn, smoke and blackened beams mark the place where travelers once stopped between the Barrens and Theramore Isle. Fire left the inn in ruins and its keeper shattered. Theramore's investigators search the wreckage for clues.",h="At the Shady Rest Inn, smoke and blackened beams mark the place where travelers once stopped between the...",sec={{t="Ashes on the Border",b="Travelers once found shelter at the Shady Rest Inn between Dustwallow Marsh and the Barrens. Then a sudden fire burned it to the ground. Innkeeper James Hyal survived, but his wife and child died in the blaze. Grief and trauma have left him with nothing. Now Theramore's authorities search the ruins for whoever lit the fire.",sp=0},{t="A Web of Suspicion",b="Early inquiries blamed human deserters and suspicious soldiers. Paval Reethe and Lieutenant Caldwell drew heavy suspicion, then met untimely ends. Hoofprints and ritual badges in the ashes revealed the attackers: ruthless Grimtotem tauren. They struck from the deep marsh to sow discord between Theramore and its neighbors.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to the Shady Rest Inn?",a="An attack burned the Shady Rest Inn to the ground. Investigators first suspected deserters and rogue Alliance soldiers, and still search the ashes for clues to the arsonists.",al={"why is shady rest inn burned","what happened to the inn","who burned shady rest"},sp=1},{q="Who owned and operated the inn?",a="James Hyal ran the Shady Rest Inn. He survived the blaze, but his wife and child died in the flames, leaving him deeply traumatized.",al={"innkeeper shady rest","who ran shady rest","james hyal"}},{q="Where is the Shady Rest Inn located?",a="The Shady Rest Inn's ruins lie beside the main road in western Dustwallow Marsh, near the border with the Barrens.",al={"shady rest location","where is shady rest inn"}},{q="Who are Paval Reethe and Lieutenant Caldwell?",a="Paval Reethe and Lieutenant Caldwell were human suspects in the early fire investigation. Both died before investigators could get confessions or learn the full extent of their involvement.",al={"who is reethe","lieutenant caldwell shady rest","reethe and caldwell"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The inn's destruction left a breach in security along the main overland route to Theramore Isle. Travelers face danger, and fears of hidden enemies are rising.",["race:Tauren"]="Suspicion over the inn fire threatens the fragile peace between the Horde and Jaina Proudmoore's forces in Dustwallow Marsh."},kw={"arson","barrens border","dustwallow marsh","grimtotem","james hyal","paval reethe","shady rest inn","theramore"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","topic:tauren"},src={"Shady Rest Inn"}}
E["subzone:stonemaul-ruins"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonemaul Ruins",z="dustwallow",s="Firemane dragonspawn hold Stonemaul Ruins, the old home of the Stonemaul ogres. Driven out by the black dragonflight, the clan fled north and left its village to the brood.",h="Firemane dragonspawn hold Stonemaul Ruins, the old home of the Stonemaul ogres.",sec={{t="Rise and Fall of the Clan Home",b="Stonemaul Village rose in the swamps of Dustwallow Marsh after the ogres came to Kalimdor. The beastmaster Rexxar won their respect by surviving the clan's deadly trials, killing their chieftain Kor'gall, and rallying the ogres to defend the young Horde against Admiral Proudmoore's forces.\n\nAfter the war, Rexxar left Mok'Morokk in command. But the ogre ruled for himself, and the village fell. Then the black dragonflight ambushed and shattered it. The survivors fled north and founded Brackenwall Village. Onyxia's brood claimed the ruins.",sp=0},{t="The Struggle for Reclamation",b="Firemane dragonspawn now infest the ruins in Dragonmurk and tend the brood's nearby nesting grounds. Overlord Mok'Morokk has grown cowardly and is content to remain in Brackenwall. Older, prouder clan members Tharg and Draz'Zilb refuse to give up their homeland. From Brackenwall, they urge Horde champions to kill the dragonspawn and smash the dragonflight's eggs. They hope the Stonemaul will march back and reclaim their ancestral village.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who used to live in Stonemaul Ruins?",a="The Stonemaul ogres built and lived in the settlement, then called Stonemaul Village, after they came to Kalimdor.",al={"who lived here","stonemaul ruins history","who built stonemaul village"}},{q="Why was the village abandoned?",a="Onyxia's black dragonflight attacked the village and drove out the ogres. Firemane dragonspawn now use the ruins as a nesting outpost.",al={"why is stonemaul destroyed","what happened to stonemaul village","who attacked stonemaul"}},{q="Where did the surviving ogres go?",a="The survivors fled north into Dustwallow Marsh and founded Brackenwall Village under Overlord Mok'Morokk.",al={"where are the ogres now","stonemaul ogre location"}},{q="What was Rexxar's connection to this place?",a="Rexxar came to enlist the ogres against Kul Tiras. He passed their trial, killed their tyrannical warlord Kor'gall, and briefly led the clan before handing command to Mok'Morokk.",al={"rexxar stonemaul","rexxar ogre chieftain"}},{q="Do the ogres plan to retake the ruins?",a="Yes. Though Mok'Morokk is afraid to act, Stonemaul leaders Tharg and Draz'Zilb recruit Horde adventurers to kill the Firemane dragonspawn and prepare to retake their home.",al={"will the ogres go back","retaking stonemaul"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you stand with Stonemaul ogres who fought beside Thrall's Horde against Kul Tiras. Helping them strike back at the black dragonflight honors that pact."},kw={"brackenwall","dragonmurk","firemane","kor'gall","mok'morokk","stonemaul","stonemaul ruins","stonemaul village"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:dragonmurk","npc:overlord-mok-morokk","npc:onyxia","topic:black-dragonflight","topic:horde","zone:dustwallow"},src={"Stonemaul Ruins"}}
E["subzone:swamplight-manor"] = {t="subzone",n="Swamplight Manor",z="dustwallow",s="In Witch Hill, 'Swamp Eye' Jarl cooks strange fare at Swamplight Manor. The crooked shack is his home, and his unusual tastes are known across the mire. Its garden draws the attention of Theramore and Brackenwall Village.",h="In Witch Hill, 'Swamp Eye' Jarl cooks strange fare at Swamplight Manor.",sec={{t="A Hermit's Respite in the Mire",b="In Witch Hill, a crooked wooden shack shelters the recluse 'Swamp Eye' Jarl. Fog, muck, and restless marsh ghosts surround his home, far from any lordly estate. Jarl lives alone and spends his days making strange local dishes from marsh creatures.\n\nTravelers come for his eccentric cooking or shelter from the spirits. Jarl also recruits them to hunt unusual ingredients, including marsh frog legs and creature eyes.",sp=0},{t="Secrets in the Garden",b="Travelers seek Jarl's cooking or shelter from Witch Hill's spirits. In his makeshift garden, a loose pile of dirt covers a discarded orcish spy's report, with a severed head nearby.\n\nTheramore's guards under Captain Garran Vimes and Horde forces at Brackenwall Village both seek the documents. The hermit's overgrown patch has become a point of tension between them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is a tiny shack called a 'Manor'?",a="The name is ironic: Swamplight Manor is a soggy, rundown wooden shack. Its reclusive inhabitant, 'Swamp Eye' Jarl, gave it the grand name against Witch Hill's dreary gloom.",al={"swamplight manor name origin","why manor","is swamplight a real manor"}},{q="Who lives at Swamplight Manor?",a="'Swamp Eye' Jarl lives alone at Swamplight Manor. The half-crazed hermit cooks strange local dishes and hires passing travelers to find peculiar ingredients and help with the local spirits.",al={"who is swamp eye jarl","swamplight manor resident","who lives here"}},{q="What is buried in the garden outside?",a="A discarded spy report penned by an orc lies beneath disturbed earth in Jarl's yard, with a severed head nearby. Theramore's Alliance authorities and Horde scouts from Brackenwall Village both seek the intelligence.",al={"swamplight manor dirt pile","loose dirt swamplight","orc spy report"},sp=1},{q="Can both Alliance and Horde players visit Jarl?",a="Yes. Jarl lives far from civilization and keeps neutral. He accepts help and trades recipes with Alliance and Horde travelers alike.",al={"is jarl neutral","can horde talk to swamp eye jarl","swamplight faction"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="For cooks who brave the marsh, Jarl is an eccentric master of swamp foraging. He makes regional meals from creatures most chefs would dread to touch.",["faction:Alliance"]="Theramore scouts sent by Captain Garran Vimes watch rumors around the manor, especially reports of missing scouts and intercepted Horde correspondence."},kw={"brackenwall village","dustwallow marsh","garran vimes","lost report","swamp eye jarl","swamplight manor","witch hill"},rel={"subzone:witch-hill","zone:dustwallow","subzone:brackenwall-village","quest:165","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Swamplight Manor"}}
E["subzone:tabetha-s-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Tabetha's Farm",z="dustwallow",s="In the Quagmire, Tabetha keeps her homestead apart from the marsh's dangers.",h="In the Quagmire, Tabetha keeps her homestead apart from the marsh's dangers.",sec={{t="A Hermit's Sanctuary",b="In western Dustwallow Marsh, a weather-worn hut, garden plots, and a dock mark the farm. The dock opens onto the swamp's waterways, while the homestead lies far from the rivalries of Theramore and Brackenwall Village. Tabetha, a reclusive human sorceress, lives here in near-total seclusion. She studies arcane and fel power beyond the reach of Dalaran and local authorities.",sp=0},{t="A Waypoint of Arcane Power",b="Mages and warlocks travel from Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms to seek Tabetha's aid. Mages come to master raw arcane surges. Warlocks ask her to help cleanse volatile artifacts such as the Orb of Orahil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives at Tabetha's Farm?",a="Tabetha, an eccentric mage, lives at the farm. She tends its garden, dock, and homestead amid the Quagmire's perilous swamp creatures.",al={"who is tabetha","who lives here","inhabitants of tabetha's farm"}},{q="Why do mages travel all the way to this farm?",a="Mage trainers across the world send promising students to Tabetha to deepen their arcane knowledge. She knows volatile mana surges, ancient relics, and primal powers rarely taught in city academies.",al={"why do mages visit tabetha","mage quest dustwallow","mage class quest tabetha"}},{q="Why would warlocks come here?",a="Warlocks seek Tabetha's knowledge of exorcism and elemental energies to purify and tame dangerous artifacts. They seek her help with the rituals that cleanse the Orb of Orahil.",al={"tabetha warlock quest","cleansing orb of orahil","warlock tabetha"}},{q="Is Tabetha's Farm allied with the Horde or the Alliance?",a="Tabetha keeps a neutral stance and shares her wisdom with travelers of any allegiance. Her farm is independent of Jaina Proudmoore's Theramore and the Horde forces at Brackenwall Village.",al={"is tabetha alliance","is tabetha horde","is tabetha neutral"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, your capital city trainers may send you to Tabetha's Farm. She can help you study volatile mana surges and ancient relics of power.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can seek Tabetha's help to cleanse the potent energies bound to the Orb of Orahil."},kw={"dustwallow","dustwallow marsh","quagmire","tabetha","tabetha's farm","tabetha's hut"},rel={"npc:tabetha","subzone:quagmire","zone:dustwallow","quest:2300","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:uldaman"},src={"Tabetha's Farm"}}
E["subzone:theramore-isle"] = {t="subzone",n="Theramore Isle",z="dustwallow",s="Theramore Isle shelters refugees from Lordaeron behind the eastern coast of Dustwallow Marsh. Lady Jaina Proudmoore founded the fortified port, now the Alliance's chief stronghold in southern Kalimdor.",h="Theramore Isle shelters refugees from Lordaeron behind the eastern coast of Dustwallow Marsh.",sec={{t="Refuge of the West",b="After the Scourge ravaged Dalaran and Lordaeron in the Third War, Lady Jaina Proudmoore led survivors across the Great Sea to Kalimdor. There, humans, dwarves, and high elves fought beside orcs and night elves to defeat the Burning Legion atop Mount Hyjal.\n\nAfter the victory, Jaina's coalition withdrew to the misty edge of Dustwallow Marsh. On an island just off the coast, they raised a harbor city with stone ramparts and Jaina's citadel, sheltering what remained of the northern kingdoms.",sp=0},{t="An Uneasy Peace",b="Theramore's peace with Thrall's Horde in neighboring Durotar has long been uneasy. When Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore arrived with the Kul Tiras fleet, he took command of the isle and began a campaign against the orcs.\n\nJaina would not let hatred undo Kalimdor's hard-won survival. She allowed the Horde to kill her father within Theramore's walls to preserve the peace. The city now holds a fragile truce with Durotar, though veteran sailors' resentment threatens to break it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules Theramore Isle?",a="Lady Jaina Proudmoore governs Theramore Isle. A master sorceress from Dalaran and Kul Tiras, she led Lordaeron's survivors to Kalimdor during the Third War. She oversees the city's defenses and diplomacy.",al={"who leads theramore","theramore ruler","jaina theramore"}},{q="Why did humans build a city in a swamp?",a="After the Battle of Mount Hyjal, the surviving human expedition needed a defensible coast to shelter its people and keep a navy. The rocky island off Dustwallow Marsh offered deep-water anchorage and separation from mainland threats, despite the bog surrounding it.",al={"why dustwallow","why is theramore in a marsh","why build here"}},{q="Is Theramore hostile to the Horde?",a="Theramore is an Alliance stronghold, and its guards meet Horde travelers with hostility. Yet Lady Jaina Proudmoore and Warchief Thrall keep an uneasy peace and respect each other's borders, despite lingering hatred among their people.",al={"can horde visit theramore","theramore horde relations","are theramore humans at war"}},{q="What happened to Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore here?",a="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore took Theramore from his daughter Jaina to make war on the young Horde. Seeing that his campaign would destroy them all, Jaina stepped aside as Thrall and Rexxar stormed the citadel and killed the Admiral in battle.",al={"daelin death","what happened to jaina's father","daelin proudmoore theramore"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Theramore Isle is the Alliance's chief seat of power in central Kalimdor. It offers safety, ferry connections, and a defended harbor amid hostile wilderness.",["class:Mage"]="As Archmage Jaina Proudmoore's home, Theramore holds powerful arcane conduits. It is a vital center of Kirin Tor tradition and teleportation in the western hemisphere."},kw={"alliance","daelin proudmoore","dustwallow marsh","jaina proudmoore","kul tiras","lordaeron refugees","theramore"},rel={"npc:jaina-proudmoore","zone:dustwallow","topic:kul-tiras","npc:thrall","topic:alliance","topic:third-war","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:ratchet"},src={"Theramore Isle"}}
E["subzone:tidefury-cove"] = {t="subzone",n="Tidefury Cove",z="dustwallow",s="Tidefury Cove’s reefs and wrecks still make these waters perilous for sailors. Makrura roam the shallows, while solitary anglers seek the quiet shore.",h="Tidefury Cove’s reefs and wrecks still make these waters perilous for sailors.",sec={{t="A Graveyard of Ships and Reefs",b="At the far end of Dustwallow Bay, Tidefury Cove lies between Theramore Isle and the Wyrmbog. Jagged reefs and shifting shoals have wrecked many vessels over the years, leaving rotting hulls half-submerged along the tide line. Makrura crawl over the wreckage, and the cove remains a dangerous, isolated shore. Hardy scavengers and quiet hermits come here to escape Theramore’s busy docks.",sp=0},{t="The Historic Foothold",b="During the invasion of Durotar, Tidefury Cove became a battleground. Admiral Daelin Proudmoore’s Kul Tiran expedition fortified the coast with a fortress and guard towers to command the approaches to Theramore. Thrall united the young Horde to break that hold. Orcs, Darkspear trolls, and tauren joined Rexxar and the Stonemaul ogres in an assault on the shore. They dismantled the Kul Tiran beachhead, then pressed toward the island fortress.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Tidefury Cove located?",a="Tidefury Cove lies on Dustwallow Marsh’s southeastern coast, south of Theramore Isle and beside the Wyrmbog coast at the southern end of Dustwallow Bay.",al={"tidefury cove location","where is tidefury cove","tidefury cove map"}},{q="Why are there shipwrecks in Tidefury Cove?",a="Shallow sandbars and hidden rocky reefs make Tidefury Cove treacherous to navigate. Ships that stray too close run aground, then waves and scavengers soon break their hulls apart.",al={"tidefury shipwrecks","broken ships tidefury","sunken ships dustwallow bay"}},{q="Who lives in Tidefury Cove today?",a="Aggressive makrura roam Tidefury Cove, and famed angler Nat Pagle keeps an encampment called Nat’s Landing on one of the outer islets.",al={"who is in tidefury cove","tidefury cove residents","nat pagle location"}},{q="What battle took place here in the past?",a="During Admiral Daelin Proudmoore’s campaign against the new Horde, Kul Tiran forces built a fortified coastal stronghold at Tidefury Cove. Thrall’s Horde, joined by tauren and ogre allies, destroyed it to clear the way to Theramore Isle.",al={"battle of tidefury cove","warcraft 3 tidefury","invasion of durotar tidefury"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, this coast was the starting point of the counter-offensive that broke Grand Admiral Proudmoore’s naval aggression and secured the young nation’s survival.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can fish the rich shallows of Dustwallow near master angler Nat Pagle, where fishermen seek prized catches."},kw={"cove","dustwallow","makrura","pagle","proudmoore","reefs","shipwreck","theramore","tidefury"},rel={"subzone:dustwallow-bay","subzone:nat-s-landing","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:wyrmbog","zone:dustwallow","npc:nat-pagle","npc:thrall","topic:horde"},src={"Tidefury Cove"}}
E["subzone:witch-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Witch Hill",z="dustwallow",s="Mirefin murlocs camp around Witch Hill, where Swamplight Manor stands near the path to Theramore. Rumors of hauntings trouble the lonely rise.",h="Mirefin murlocs camp around Witch Hill, where Swamplight Manor stands near the path to Theramore.",sec={{t="A Blighted Rise",b="Witch Hill rises from the waters of Dustwallow Marsh, about a third of the way down the peninsula toward Theramore Isle. Mirefin murlocs claim the waters around it, and their camps make the swamp dangerous. Near the hill's center stands Swamplight Manor, home to the hermit known as 'Swamp Eye' Jarl. Travelers report eerie sights and dark presences across the rise.",sp=0},{t="The Haunting of the Hill",b="Rumors of hauntings cling to Witch Hill's desolate ground. Mirefin murlocs are not the only danger there. Occult threats trouble the hill, and even Theramore patrols find it unsettling.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Witch Hill located?",a="Witch Hill lies in Dustwallow Marsh, about a third of the way down the peninsula that runs from the western marsh toward Theramore Isle.",al={"witch hill location","where is witch hill","how to find witch hill"}},{q="Who lives on Witch Hill?",a="'Swamp Eye' Jarl lives in Swamplight Manor near the hill's center. Mirefin murlocs camp in the surrounding lowlands.",al={"who lives here","witch hill inhabitants","swamplight manor resident"}},{q="Why is the area called Witch Hill?",a="Witch Hill has a sinister reputation for dark magic, odd lights, and supernatural danger. Swamplight Manor's eerie solitude adds to its name.",al={"why witch hill","is there a witch here","witch hill lore"},sp=1},{q="What threats should travelers look out for on Witch Hill?",a="Watch for Mirefin murlocs camping around Witch Hill, and heed the rumors of hauntings on the rise.",al={"witch hill dangers","witch hill enemies","mobs on witch hill"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may sense the rumors of hauntings clinging to Witch Hill as you travel the road toward Theramore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Witch Hill borders the main overland route toward Theramore Isle, where murloc tribes and dark entities trouble travelers and couriers."},kw={"dustwallow marsh","mirefin","swamp eye jarl","swamplight manor","witch hill"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:swamplight-manor","topic:murloc"},src={"Witch Hill"}}
E["subzone:wyrmbog"] = {t="subzone",n="Wyrmbog",z="dustwallow",s="Black dragons hold Wyrmbog, south of the Dragonmurk in Dustwallow Marsh. Their caves cut into the ridges, where Onyxia and Emberstrife keep their lairs.",h="Black dragons hold Wyrmbog, south of the Dragonmurk in Dustwallow Marsh.",sec={{t="Heart of the Brood",b="Black dragons patrol the scorched mire beneath towering bones. Whelps and mature drakes fill the air, while toxic fumes and wild beasts make the bog perilous to cross. Onyxia's Lair and Emberstrife's cavernous den lie within these reaches. The black dragonflight holds the southern marsh, and few travelers can pass safely through its territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Wyrmbog?",a="Wyrmbog lies south of the Dragonmurk in Dustwallow Marsh, where black dragons hold the marshland.",al={"wyrmbog","what is wyrmbog","where is wyrmbog"}},{q="Which dragons dwell in Wyrmbog?",a="Black dragonkin, drakes, and whelps patrol Wyrmbog. Emberstrife and the broodmother Onyxia keep lairs along its southern edge.",al={"who lives in wyrmbog","dragons in wyrmbog","what dragons are here"}},{q="Where is Onyxia's Lair located in relation to Wyrmbog?",a="Onyxia's Lair opens among the rocky spires and caves along Wyrmbog's southern edge.",al={"onyxia lair location","where is onyxia","entrance to onyxia"}},{q="Who is Emberstrife?",a="Emberstrife is an ancient black dragon who lives in a cave among Wyrmbog's rocky ridges and guards the broodmother's territory.",al={"emberstrife","who is emberstrife","emberstrifes den"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion hunting the black dragonflight, you find Wyrmbog the last staging ground before Onyxia's threshold.",["faction:Horde"]="Warchief Thrall's scouts watch Wyrmbog closely. Black dragons nest near the Barrens and Theramore, threatening Kalimdor's fragile balance."},kw={"black dragonflight","dragonmurk","drakes","dustwallow","emberstrife","marsh","onyxia","wyrmbog"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:onyxia-s-lair","subzone:dragonmurk","topic:black-dragonflight","npc:onyxia"},src={"Wyrmbog"}}
E["zone:dustwallow"] = {t="zone",n="Dustwallow Marsh",z="dustwallow",s="Across central Kalimdor, Dustwallow Marsh lies between the Barrens and the Great Sea. Underground springs feed its treacherous fens, where dangerous predators, covert faction skirmishes, and the black dragonflight all lurk. To the east, theramore isle is an Alliance fortress; to the northwest, Horde-allied Stonemaul ogres hold Brackenwall Village.",h="Across central Kalimdor, Dustwallow Marsh lies between the Barrens and the Great Sea.",sec={{t="A Drowned Landscape",b="Before the Great Sundering, Dustwallow was a high, grassy plain where herds roamed. The cataclysm shattered the valley and raised the water table, drowning the land in endless stagnant pools, mossy shallows, and choking mud.\n\nUnderground springs keep the marsh humid and submerged beneath thick fog. Crocolisks, raptors, and spiders haunt the fens. Crumbling causeways cross them, but jagged shallows and wandering bogs make every step beyond those roads perilous.",sp=0},{t="Old Hatreds and Uneasy Truces",b="Dustwallow stayed largely wild until after the Third War, when Lady Jaina Proudmoore led human refugees across the sea and founded the citadel of Theramore Isle on the eastern coast. Soon, Kul Tiran forces under Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore fought Thrall's fledgling Horde in bloody battles across the wetlands. The Admiral was defeated, and Theramore and Orgrimmar now keep an official armistice.\n\nTension still smolders. Theramore faces desertions and sabotage, while spies wage quiet, deadly conflicts across the fens.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow of the Wyrmbog",b="In southern Dustwallow, rocky ground rises into the Dragonmurk and Wyrmbog. The Stonemaul ogres first settled there under Rexxar, their half-ogre champion, until the black dragonflight drove them violently from Stonemaul Village. The displaced ogres fled north to Brackenwall Village under Overlord Mok'Morokk and swore vengeance.\n\nOnyxia, daughter of Deathwing, lurks among the jagged crags. She directs her brood and weaves sinister machinations far beyond the swamp.",sp=2}},faq={{q="What is the main Alliance settlement here?",a="The Alliance's main settlement is Theramore Isle, a fortified city-state on a rocky island off the eastern coast. Lady Jaina Proudmoore founded it after the Third War. A narrow roadway links it to Kalimdor, and vital ship routes run to Menethil Harbor in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"alliance base dustwallow","where is theramore","human town dustwallow"}},{q="Where can Horde adventurers find refuge in the swamp?",a="Horde travelers find refuge at Brackenwall Village in the marsh's northwest. The Stonemaul ogres founded the settlement, joined the Horde under Rexxar, and opened their gates to orcish and tauren allies.",al={"horde base dustwallow","where is brackenwall","ogre village"}},{q="Why are there so many black dragons in the southern marsh?",a="Black dragons gather in the southern marsh because the Wyrmbog and Dragonmurk are Onyxia's domain and brood grounds. Her black dragonspawn drove out the Stonemaul ogres and made nests for whelps and drakes among the rocky outcroppings and deep caves.",al={"wyrmbog dragons","why black dragons here","dragonmurk"},sp=2},{q="What happened to the Stonemaul ogres' original home?",a="The Stonemaul ogres once lived peacefully in Stonemaul Village in the southern marsh. The black dragonflight attacked, slaughtering many and forcing the survivors to flee northwest to Brackenwall Village.",al={"stonemaul ruins","what happened to stonemaul village","old ogre town"}},{q="Who lives in the lonely cottage out in the Quagmire?",a="Tabetha owns the cottage and lives quietly as an eccentric, powerful hermit mage in the marsh's depths. Arcane practitioners seek her instruction or help cleansing volatile magical relics.",al={"tabetha's farm","tabetha dustwallow","who is the witch in the swamp"}},{q="What is Alcaz Island and who controls it?",a="Strashaz naga control Alcaz Island, a heavily guarded isle off the marsh's northeast coast. Dangerous elite defenders patrol it, and hydras lurk in the surrounding waters.",al={"alcaz island","island off coast dustwallow","what is on alcaz"},sp=2}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Theramore Isle is the heart of the Alliance's presence on Kalimdor. Arriving via menethil harbor, you guard its causeways while untangling a web of deserters and missing envoys.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde emissaries come to support the beleaguered Stonemaul ogres at Brackenwall Village. You help repel dragon incursions from the Wyrmbog and keep a wary eye on human movements along the coast.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may cross the fens to Tabetha's Farm in the Quagmire. The recluse offers unique expertise on arcane conduits and ancient power sources."},kw={"alcaz","brackenwall","dustwallow","jaina","marsh","onyxia","quagmire","stonemaul","tabetha","theramore","wyrmbog"},rel={"subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:onyxia-s-lair","subzone:wyrmbog","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","subzone:tabetha-s-farm","quest:1241"},src={"Dustwallow Marsh (Classic)","Dustwallow Marsh"}}
